WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:05.710
and welcome to your second drink of The Job Part 1.
欢迎收听《办公室》播客关于《工作（上集）》的第二杯饮品。

2
00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:08.550
Paul Lieberstein joined us for the top of this episode.
保罗·利伯斯坦做客了本集节目的前半段。

3
00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:11.670
You know, he wrote this episode along with Mike Schur.
你知道的，这集是和他以及迈克·舒尔共同编剧的。

4
00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:12.890
What a dynamic duo.
真是个梦幻般的双人组。

5
00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:13.590
Right?
对吧？

6
00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:15.150
This was a great interview.
这是一场极棒的访谈。

7
00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:17.270
We got to hear all about how he came to play Toby.
我们听到了他如何开始饰演托比的种种趣事。

8
00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:19.550
Yeah, and he gave some really fun facts
对，他还透露了一些非常有趣的事实

9
00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:21.190
about this episode as well.
同样也是关于这一集的。

10
00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:25.650
So The Job Part 1 ran as a special hour-long
所以《工作（上集）》作为一小时的特别版

11
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:29.050
season three finale episode along with The Job Part 2.
第三季季终集与《工作（下集）》一同播出。

12
00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:32.430
But you know, it was actually only 40 minutes.
但你知道的，其实它只有40分钟。

13
00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:33.470
With commercials.
算上广告的话。

14
00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:36.810
Well, the super fan episode for The Job 1 and 2
嗯，《工作》一和二的超级粉丝加长版

15
00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:41.510
is over an hour long, a real hour, no commercials.
时长超过一小时，实打实的一个小时，没有广告。

16
00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:43.590
That's like a mini The Office movie.
这就好比是一部迷你的《办公室》电影。

17
00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:46.830
Yes, it's almost like they added a third episode.
没错，感觉就像他们加拍了第三集一样。

18
00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:52.250
And there is a very big thing that was added back to the cold open.
而且片头冷开场里加回了一个非常重大的内容。

19
00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:54.650
We kind of talked about it in our breakdown.
我们在解析节目时稍微聊过这个。

20
00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:56.890
You know, in The Job Part 2,
你知道的，在《工作（下集）》里

21
00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.870
when Jim is being interviewed by David Wallace,
当吉姆接受大卫·华莱士的面试时

22
00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:05.070
and there's a little flashback to the beach games episode.
有一个海滩游戏那一集的小闪回。

23
00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:08.770
And Jim tells Pam why he left Scranton.
吉姆向帕姆倾诉了他离开斯克兰顿的原因。

24
00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:09.890
To go to Stanford.
去斯坦福。

25
00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:10.470
Yes.
是的。

26
00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:10.730
Yeah.
没错。

27
00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.970
Well, when we first discussed this episode,
好吧，当我们最初讨论这一集时

28
00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:17.230
we talked about that flashback scene at the beach for Jim and Pam.
我们谈到了吉姆和帕姆在海滩上的那个闪回场景。

29
00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:22.390
And we said that it was originally going to be the cold open for this episode.
当时我们说它原本是这一集的冷开场。

30
00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:25.310
Well, we got it a little wrong, lady.
好吧，我们稍微搞错了，女士。

31
00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:26.710
It can happen.
这也是难免的。

32
00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:27.390
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

33
00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:28.490
So give me the scoop.
所以，快跟我说说内幕吧。

34
00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:32.850
Well, the scene during Jim's interview was always meant to be there.
好吧，吉姆面试时的那个场景本来就计划放在那里的。

35
00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:33.590
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

36
00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:38.510
There was a different part of that scene on the beach between Jim and Pam
吉姆和帕姆在海滩上的那个场景中，有另一个部分

37
00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:40.530
that would have been the cold open.
原本是打算做冷开场的。

38
00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:44.170
And I didn't realize that when we first broke down the episode.
我们在初次解析这一集时并没有意识到这一点。

39
00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:48.230
They have put that cold open back into the super fan episode.
他们把那个冷开场重新剪回了超级粉丝版里。

40
00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:52.950
It totally kicks off Pam's, like, new direct way of communicating.
这完全开启了帕姆那种崭新的、直率的沟通方式。

41
00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:54.890
You have to hear it.
你一定要听听看。

42
00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:57.330
Hey, I'm really sorry that I didn't come to your art show.
嘿，我真的很抱歉我没去看你的艺术展。

43
00:01:58.670 --> 00:01:59.190
Okay.
好的。

44
00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:01.790
Is that all you heard?
你听到的就只有这个吗？

45
00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:02.970
Because I said some other stuff.
因为我还说了别的一些话。

46
00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:04.530
Really?
真的吗？

47
00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:05.850
I don't know.
我不知道。

48
00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:08.950
You know what's interesting?
你知道有趣的是什么吗？

49
00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:11.470
I don't feel embarrassed.
我一点也不觉得尴尬。

50
00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:12.950
At all.
完全不觉得。

51
00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:15.970
I just feel good.
我只是感觉很好。

52
00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:19.060
Good.
很好。

53
00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:30.400
If you don't have anything to say, you don't have to say anything.
如果你没什么想说的，你可以什么都不说。

54
00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:36.150
Or no, I take that back.
或者不对，我收回刚才的话。

55
00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:39.010
You have to say something.
你必须说点什么。

56
00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:46.360
You guys, I'm doing it!
伙计们，我成功了！

57
00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:48.960
I'm walking on boiling steam!
我在沸腾的蒸汽上行走！

58
00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:55.010
How can you even think about leaving that?
你怎么能舍得离开那个？

59
00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:57.350
Hey, can anybody see this?
嘿，有人能看到这个吗？

60
00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:01.420
I mean, does he just sit there silent the whole time?
我是说，他难道就一直坐在那儿不说话吗？

61
00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:01.960
Yeah.
对。

62
00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:04.840
I really liked how she was like, is that all you're going to respond to?
我很喜欢她当时那种“你就打算回这个吗”的态度。

63
00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:05.980
Because I said some other stuff.
因为我还说了一些别的事。

64
00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:06.380
Yeah.
对。

65
00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.380
She does not let him off the hook.
她可真是一点都不放过他。

66
00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:09.100
Go Pam.
干得好，帕姆。

67
00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:13.160
So I traded messages with Dave Rogers about these flashbacks.
所以我跟戴夫·罗杰斯交流了关于这些闪回画面的信息。

68
00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:17.360
And he said that this is one of his single favorite moments of the show.
他说这是整部剧里他最喜欢的片段之一。

69
00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:24.000
Because it's one of those rare things where even the way it was in the original broadcast really
因为这是那种罕见的情况，哪怕是最初播出的形式，也真正

70
00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:30.620
illuminated the creative freedom that the documentary filmmakers have when they are deciding what
展现了纪录片制作人在决定他们

71
00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:32.160
they want to show and when.
想要展示什么以及何时展示时所拥有的创作自由。

72
00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:33.220
Sure.
确实。

73
00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:37.600
I mean, they can tell a completely different version of a moment through editing.
我的意思是，他们可以通过剪辑讲出一个完全不同版本的时刻。

74
00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:40.460
And that's true even when you watch reality TV today.
哪怕你现在看真人秀节目，也是如此。

75
00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:41.120
Yes!
没错！

76
00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:46.080
He said that they talked a lot about this in the edit that they decided to use.
他说他们在最终采用的剪辑版本中讨论了很多这个。

77
00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:50.640
Like, the portion of this flashback footage that they decided to use in the job part two.
比如，他们决定在《工作》（第二部分）里使用的这部分闪回素材。

78
00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:54.720
They really tried to put themselves in the mindset of the documentary crew.
他们真的努力让自己代入纪录片摄制组的心态。

79
00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:58.140
Originally, they settled on just having the one little clip.
最初，他们决定只保留一个小片段。

80
00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:01.920
Also, in the episode when Pam has her talking head at the top of this episode,
另外，在本集开头帕姆进行单独采访时，

81
00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:06.200
you see just sort of like a flashback to this conversation with no audio.
你可以看到类似闪回到这段对话的无声画面。

82
00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:10.400
And Pam just says, Jim was nice, told me that he missed our friendship too.
然后帕姆只是说，吉姆人很好，告诉我他也怀念我们的友谊。

83
00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:12.460
And then they kind of hug and walk off.
接着他们拥抱了一下，然后走开了。

84
00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:16.180
And then Dave said again, when they had this bigger chunk of the scene,
然后戴夫再次提到，当他们有了这一大段场景时，

85
00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:20.300
they had to discuss again, like, where would the documentary crew put this?
他们不得不再次讨论，比如，纪录片摄制组会把这个放在哪里？

86
00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:23.120
Where would it make the most sense to put this?
把它放在哪里才最合乎情理？

87
00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.300
And they decided to put it back up at the top.
于是他们决定把它放回开头。

88
00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:28.220
I just love Dave's insight on everything.
我太喜欢戴夫对所有事情的见解了。

89
00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:29.200
I know, lady.
我知道，姐妹。

90
00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:30.700
I wrote him an email about it where I said,
我为此给他写了一封邮件，我说，

91
00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:33.640
oh, can you tell me about these flashback scenes to beach games?
噢，你能跟我讲讲这些关于沙滩游戏的闪回场景吗？

92
00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:35.680
And the beginning of his email was,
他邮件的开头是，

93
00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:39.000
get ready for a Dave Rogers dissertation or just give me a call.
准备好迎接戴夫·罗杰斯的超长论述吧，或者直接给我打个电话。

94
00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:45.000
Well, I also wanted to share a scene that was added back to the super fan episode.
嗯，我还想分享一个被加回超长粉丝版剧集里的场景。

95
00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:47.040
I had mentioned it in our breakdown.
我在我们的解析里提到过它。

96
00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:49.280
It's the runner of Dwight interviewing Andy.
就是德怀特采访安迪的那条副线。

97
00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:49.740
Yes.
是的。

98
00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:52.560
So the stuff that was included in the episode is so funny.
所以节目里收录的内容真的太搞笑了。

99
00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:55.560
And I mentioned that there was a lot more in the deleted scenes.
我提到过删除片段里还有很多内容。

100
00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:57.260
We didn't play it before.
我们之前没播过。

101
00:04:57.260 --> 00:04:59.280
And I just thought it would be so fun to hear it.
我只是觉得听这个会非常有意思。

102
00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:03.140
So here are the extra interview questions that got added back
所以这里是那些被加回到

103
00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:04.600
to the super fan episode.
超级粉丝版剧集中的额外采访问题。

104
00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:09.840
What is 879 times 413.7?
879乘以413.7是多少？

105
00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:16.480
2,401.647 repeating.
2,401.647循环。

106
00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:19.080
Inventor of the cotton gin, Eli Edison.
轧棉机的发明者，伊利·爱迪生。

107
00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:20.900
When is the Paleolithic age?
旧石器时代是什么时候？

108
00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.120
17 BC.
公元前17年。

109
00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:24.000
Who's the second man on the moon?
谁是第二个登上月球的人？

110
00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:24.840
Trick question.
陷阱题。

111
00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:27.640
There was no second man on the moon.
根本没有第二个登上月球的人。

112
00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:29.940
Talk me through an appendectomy.
跟我讲讲阑尾切除术的步骤。

113
00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:31.820
Step one, disinfection.
第一步，消毒。

114
00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:33.360
Step two, incision.
第二步，切口。

115
00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:39.860
Step three, remove the appendix tenderly so it doesn't burst and spread toxic-icity everywhere.
第三步，温柔地取出阑尾，这样它才不会破裂并把毒素到处扩散。

116
00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:42.560
Step four, the ectomy procedure.
第四步，“切除”手术程序。

117
00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:46.160
Step five, re-sutures.
第五步，重新缝合。

118
00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:46.300
Re-sutures.
重新缝合。

119
00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:47.580
Re-sutures, yes.
重新缝合，是的。

120
00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.400
What is the origin of species?
物种起源是什么？

121
00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:50.680
How far away is Venus?
金星有多远？

122
00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:52.580
Define scorched earth policy.
解释焦土政策。

123
00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:53.500
How do you please a woman?
如何取悦女人？

124
00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:54.900
What is a scented candle?
什么是香薰蜡烛？

125
00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:56.260
What is the Dharma initiative?
什么是达摩计划？

126
00:05:56.260 --> 00:06:00.360
It is the source of all energy on this planet.
它是这个星球上所有能量的源泉。

127
00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.380
It is a corporation formed by aliens.
它是由外星人成立的公司。

128
00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:06.420
You just know our writers had so much fun.
你知道我们的编剧们当时玩得有多开心。

129
00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:10.500
I mean, especially that little section of where you're just hearing the questions.
我是说，尤其是那段只能听到提问的小片段。

130
00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:14.040
I mean, I know that was like on the day pitches.
我是说，我知道那就像是当天的现场提案。

131
00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:14.760
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

132
00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:16.320
I don't know how Rain got through that.
我不知道雷恩是怎么撑过那一段的。

133
00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:17.680
I'm sure he didn't.
我敢说他根本没撑过去。

134
00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:19.600
I'm sure there's footage of him cracking up.
我确信有他笑场时的素材。

135
00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:25.720
Well, finally, Angela, we talked a lot about the Jim-Pam-Karen relationship in this episode.
好的，安吉拉，最后，我们在这一集中聊了很多关于吉姆、帕姆和凯伦关系的话题。

136
00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:26.040
Yeah.
是的。

137
00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:28.540
And we got a letter from Lindsey C.
我们收到了林赛·C.的一封信

138
00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:29.460
who said,
信中说：

139
00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:32.700
If there is ever a second drink episode of The Job,
如果以后还有关于《工作》第二季的喝一杯播客节目，

140
00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:38.180
I just wanted to throw out another possible point of view of Jim's reactions to Karen in this episode.
我只是想提出关于吉姆在这一集中对凯伦反应的另一个可能视角。

141
00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:43.100
I feel like Jim has never been fully 100% committed to this relationship
我觉得吉姆从来没有百分之百地投入到这段感情中，

142
00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:47.900
and was often put out with Karen and maybe even looking for ways to brush her off.
而且经常对凯伦感到不耐烦，甚至可能在寻找打发她的方法。

143
00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:50.600
For example, right before Roy's attack,
比如，就在罗伊袭击之前，

144
00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:55.600
Karen is talking to him about how he'd rather stay home and watch a Phillies game than go out with her.
凯伦正在和他谈论他宁愿在家看费城人队的比赛也不愿和她出去约会的事。

145
00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:58.580
Like you've both said before, we all love Jim, of course,
正如你们俩之前都说过的那样，我们当然都爱吉姆，

146
00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:02.160
but a lot of times throughout this relationship, it really does bring out his worSt.
但在整段感情中，很多时候这确实暴露了他最糟糕的一面。

147
00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:07.760
So when Jim had the talking head explaining his haircut and Karen's snarky comment about him looking homeless,
所以当吉姆对着单采镜头解释他的发型，以及凯伦讽刺他看起来像个流浪汉时，

148
00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:11.640
I think he was truly offended by it and holding on to a bit of a grudge.
我认为他是真的被冒犯了，并且一直记恨在心。

149
00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:16.740
Then when in New York, instead of giving Karen any kind of answer about moving with her
然后到了纽约，比起给凯伦任何关于和她一起搬家，

150
00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:21.460
or about one too many people in New York, I think it's because he is truly conflicted.
或者关于纽约人太多了的明确答复，我认为是因为他真的很纠结。

151
00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:23.960
He is on this trip trying to enjoy their relationship,
他这次旅行试图享受他们的关系，

152
00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:27.540
but having to really search for the happiness that it should be providing.
但却不得不极力去寻找这种关系本该带来的快乐。

153
00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:32.420
So then when he finds the beloved yogurt lid and Karen has just ditched him for her girlfriends,
