所以我们讨论了角色的分配——当时有明蒂、B·J、我和迈克。

305
00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:49.630
And then there was a couple consultants, there was Lester and Larry.
然后还有几个顾问，莱斯特和拉里。

306
00:14:51.190 --> 00:14:54.230
So the four of us each got, like, little roles.
所以我们四个人每个人都分到了一些小角色。

307
00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:59.070
I guess Mike's didn't come on – most didn't start that season.
我猜迈克的没有播——大多数在那一季还没有开始。

308
00:14:59.730 --> 00:15:05.330
But – so we had talked about just doing a little thing to kind of have the experience
不过——所以我们讨论过只是做个小尝试，为了体验一下

309
00:15:05.330 --> 00:15:11.030
of being an actor, and hopefully it would inform our writing.
当演员的感觉，希望这能对我们的编剧工作有所启发。

310
00:15:11.090 --> 00:15:13.730
So here he wanted to kind of, like, break that down together.
所以在这里，他有点想一起把那个打破。

311
00:15:13.730 --> 00:15:18.890
So I feel like – I'm not sure how Toey happened, but I feel like I left the room
所以我觉得——我不太确定托比是怎么来的，但我感觉我离开了房间

312
00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:22.710
and I came back and they said, you're going to play this part.
然后我回来时他们说，你要演这个角色。

313
00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:30.090
And it was one line, you know, in Diversity Day about, you know, I say this one line
那只有一句台词，你知道的，在《多元化日》里，你知道的，我说这句台词

314
00:15:30.090 --> 00:15:31.190
and get kicked out of the room.
然后就被赶出了房间。

315
00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:36.610
Now, I heard, Paul, and you tell me if this is true, I heard that at the table read,
现在，我听说，保罗，你告诉我这是不是真的，我听说在剧本围读时，

316
00:15:36.770 --> 00:15:42.970
they had you read that line and that Steve, as Michael, jumped on you so viciously
他们让你读了那句台词，史蒂夫饰演的迈克尔极其凶猛地扑向你，

317
00:15:42.970 --> 00:15:48.010
and everyone erupted in laughter because you sort of almost reacted a little bit as yourself
每个人都爆发出笑声，因为你的反应有点像是你本人，

318
00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:51.890
and a little bit maybe how you thought Tobey might, you know, but you still didn't know
又有点像是你觉得托比可能会有的反应，你知道的，但你当时还不知道

319
00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:53.750
who Tobey was at that moment, right?
那一刻托比是谁，对吧？

320
00:15:53.830 --> 00:15:55.590
You're still discovering who is Tobey.
你还在发掘托比究竟是谁。

321
00:15:55.770 --> 00:16:01.730
There were early table reads where it was just for, like, weird contractual reasons,
早期的剧本围读有些只是因为一些奇怪的合同原因，

322
00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:04.510
just the main five actors.
只有主要的五位演员。

323
00:16:04.530 --> 00:16:06.690
And I was reading Kevin.
而我在读凯文的词。

324
00:16:06.970 --> 00:16:08.810
Yeah, you read a few roles.
对，你读过好几个角色。

325
00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:09.410
Yeah.
对。

326
00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:11.110
And I think I did well.
而且我觉得我表现得不错。

327
00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:12.590
I think I got laughs as Kevin.
我觉得我作为凯文逗笑了大家。

328
00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:17.490
I think that the supporting cast wasn't there because you were guest stars and you were not
我想配角当时不在是因为你们是客串演员，你们不是

329
00:16:18.090 --> 00:16:19.010
series regular.
常规演员。

330
00:16:19.270 --> 00:16:22.810
So in a series regular contract, you're required to do the table read.
所以根据常规演员合同，你们是必须参加剧本围读的。

331
00:16:22.810 --> 00:16:28.070
It's part of your acting deal, but I think they have to pay you more.
这是你们演员工资协议的一部分，不过我想他们必须付给你们更多钱。

332
00:16:28.230 --> 00:16:29.790
Oh, to attend those?
哦，出席那些吗？

333
00:16:29.990 --> 00:16:32.190
If you don't have that kind of contract.
如果你没有那种合同的话。

334
00:16:32.530 --> 00:16:33.390
That sounds right.
听起来确实如此。

335
00:16:33.710 --> 00:16:33.890
Yeah.
对。

336
00:16:34.010 --> 00:16:38.490
You know, it's interesting because I, as a guest star, they say you're invited.
你知道，这很有趣，因为我作为一个客串演员，他们说你是受邀出席的。

337
00:16:38.770 --> 00:16:39.050
Yeah.
对。

338
00:16:39.250 --> 00:16:39.430
Right?
是吧？

339
00:16:39.590 --> 00:16:40.470
Not required.
不是必须的。

340
00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:42.590
You're invited if you would like to come.
如果你想来，你是受邀的。

341
00:16:42.710 --> 00:16:43.390
And I always do.
而我总是会去。

342
00:16:43.490 --> 00:16:44.930
But I think you're right, Jenna.
但我觉得你是对的，珍娜。

343
00:16:45.110 --> 00:16:48.130
It wasn't until after Booze Cruise that we started coming to table reads.
直到《酒鬼游轮》之后，我们才开始参加剧本围读。

344
00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:48.930
Yeah.
对。

345
00:16:48.930 --> 00:16:54.750
So, Paul, you read a bunch of roles and everyone laughed when Michael jumped on you as Toby.
所以，保罗，你读了一堆角色，当迈克尔把托比扑倒时大家都笑了。

346
00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:56.630
And I feel like that helped seal the deal.
我觉得这有助于板上钉钉。

347
00:16:56.850 --> 00:16:59.090
But we also didn't expect that part to come back ever.
但我们也没想到那个角色以后还会再出现。

348
00:16:59.690 --> 00:17:00.970
Oh, that's how they got you.
哦，他们就是这样套牢你的。

349
00:17:01.210 --> 00:17:04.310
That's what Mike Schur said about Moe's.
迈克·舒尔对莫斯也是这么说的。

350
00:17:04.390 --> 00:17:07.350
It was just supposed to be a silly photo, you know?
那本来只应该是一张搞笑的照片，你知道的？

351
00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:08.070
Yeah.
对。

352
00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:08.470
Yeah.
对。

353
00:17:08.610 --> 00:17:08.990
That's right.
没错。

354
00:17:08.990 --> 00:17:10.150
He started as a photo.
他一开始只是一张照片。

355
00:17:10.730 --> 00:17:15.830
And then years later, he had to walk around with that beard for like a whole year, a whole
然后几年后，他不得不留着那胡子走来走去，差不多整整一年，整整

356
00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:19.050
season because Greg wouldn't let him use a fake one.
一季，因为格雷格不让他用假胡子。

357
00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:22.750
And it all started because he was just going to be in a photo.
而这一切都只是因为他本来只需要出现在一张照片里。

358
00:17:23.050 --> 00:17:25.290
And then the fake one looked better, I think.
然后我觉得，假胡子看起来反而更好。

359
00:17:25.590 --> 00:17:25.910
Yes.
是的。

360
00:17:26.030 --> 00:17:30.750
And then he was furious because he had had that huge beard and the fake one worked just
然后他气坏了，因为他留了那么大一撮胡子，结果假胡子效果

361
00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:31.270
as well.
一样很好。

362
00:17:33.050 --> 00:17:36.410
Well, Paul, how was that experience?
保罗，那次经历感觉怎么样？

363
00:17:36.810 --> 00:17:37.850
Was Greg right?
格雷格是对的吗？

364
00:17:38.050 --> 00:17:41.890
Did you feel like you learned from the experience of being an actor?
你觉得自己从当演员的经历中学到了东西吗？

365
00:17:42.170 --> 00:17:43.470
I absolutely did.
我绝对学到了。

366
00:17:43.570 --> 00:17:45.050
But it took a while to get there.
但过程花了一点时间。

367
00:17:45.050 --> 00:17:49.190
I don't know if you remember, but we were doing this kind of room bit about like my acting
我不知道你记不记得，当时我们搞了一个关于我的表演

368
00:17:49.190 --> 00:17:49.630
school.
学校的烂梗。

369
00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:52.750
I do remember your acting school bit.
我确实记得你那个表演学校的梗。

370
00:17:52.990 --> 00:17:53.330
It's okay.
没关系。

371
00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:56.330
So imagine going into acting, knowing nothing about acting.
所以想象一下，对演戏一无所知就去演戏。

372
00:17:56.470 --> 00:18:01.990
And the first thing you're being taught is take your water bottle off your desk and
而你学到的第一件事就是把水杯从桌子上拿下来，

373
00:18:01.990 --> 00:18:03.030
put it underneath your desk.
放到桌子底下。

374
00:18:03.030 --> 00:18:05.130
So because the label isn't cleared.
就因为商标没有遮掉。

375
00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:06.230
All right.
好吧。

376
00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:09.330
That's now the first thing I know about acting, you know?
这就是我关于演戏知道的第一件事，你知道吗？

377
00:18:09.470 --> 00:18:12.670
And it was like things like that that made up my acting school.
诸如此类的事情构成了我的表演学校。

378
00:18:13.670 --> 00:18:14.550
I remember.
我记得。

379
00:18:15.230 --> 00:18:18.510
Also, I remember Rain would just ride you so hard.
另外，我记得雷恩对你要求特别严格。

380
00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:19.650
Like you go, hey, Kate.
比如你说，嘿，凯特。

381
00:18:19.750 --> 00:18:20.750
And she goes, hey, Paul.
然后她说，嘿，保罗。

382
00:18:21.090 --> 00:18:22.410
And you're like, dang it.
然后你就想，可恶。

383
00:18:22.810 --> 00:18:26.390
Because she was supposed to be Meredith in the moment you're in a scene.
因为只要你进了一个场景，她就得是梅雷迪思。

384
00:18:26.690 --> 00:18:26.740
Yeah.
对。

385
00:18:26.740 --> 00:18:29.370
And I remember Rain would like tease you so hard.
而且我记得雷恩会狠狠地逗你。

386
00:18:32.050 --> 00:18:34.310
Yeah, there was very little acting I was doing.
对，我其实没怎么在演戏。

387
00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:36.530
There was a breakthrough moment for me.
对我来说有一个突破的时刻。

388
00:18:36.770 --> 00:18:38.850
They kept saying, talk louder.
他们一直说，大声点。

389
00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:40.130
And I wouldn't.
而我偏不。

390
00:18:40.450 --> 00:18:43.690
We were like, no, I'm talking to a person right here.
我们当时想，不，我就在跟旁边这个人说话。

391
00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:44.870
Why would I talk louder?
我为什么要大声说话？

392
00:18:46.130 --> 00:18:49.730
You just rolled out multicams for yourself, but that's okay.
你刚才自己顺便用了多机位视角，不过没关系。

393
00:18:50.310 --> 00:18:50.790
Yeah.
对。

394
00:18:50.970 --> 00:18:51.470
And theater.
还有戏剧。

395
00:18:51.890 --> 00:18:52.490
All in theater.
全都是戏剧。

396
00:18:52.490 --> 00:18:56.930
And then so we were doing a kitchen scene and they kept telling me to speak up.
然后我们在拍一场厨房的戏，他们一直叫我大声说。

397
00:18:57.170 --> 00:19:01.730
And then Brian said, why don't you imagine like this room is artificially quiet because
接着布莱恩说，你为什么不想象这个房间由于

398
00:19:01.730 --> 00:19:03.650
they turned off the refrigerator, right?
他们关掉了冰箱而变得出奇的安静，对吧？

399
00:19:04.010 --> 00:19:04.630
Because of the sound.
就因为收音问题。

400
00:19:05.010 --> 00:19:07.410
Why don't you imagine that the refrigerator's on?
你为什么不想象冰箱其实开着呢？

401
00:19:07.650 --> 00:19:08.590
And you have to talk about it.
而且你必须谈论它。

402
00:19:12.110 --> 00:19:15.210
Oh, an actor does that.
哦，演员就是这么做的。

403
00:19:16.010 --> 00:19:19.790
You know, it put this like, and it wasn't just like one little thing.
你知道，它就像是这样，而且不只是一件小事。

404
00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:26.550
It was like, oh, an actor has to put all these, all those little details.
就像是，哦，演员必须把所有这些、所有那些微小的细节都放进去。

405
00:19:26.690 --> 00:19:29.650
It has to justify anything that needs to be done.
它必须合理解释任何需要完成的事情。

406
00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:31.570
They don't just do what feels real.
他们不只是做感觉真实的事。

407
00:19:31.750 --> 00:19:35.670
They have to like find a way to do what they need to do and make it feel real.
他们必须想方设法去做他们需要做的事，并让它感觉真实。

408
00:19:35.810 --> 00:19:36.910
I love hearing that.
我很高兴听到这个。

409
00:19:37.130 --> 00:19:41.790
Is this something that you've brought to other projects, Paul, as a writer, showrunner,
保罗，作为一名编剧、剧集运作人、

410
00:19:41.790 --> 00:19:46.750
creator of shows, have you asked your writing staff to act at all?
剧集主创，你是否把这一点带到过其他项目中，你有没有要求你的编剧团队去表演？

411
00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:47.630
I did.
我做过。

412
00:19:48.030 --> 00:19:49.030
Let's see, I'm ghosted.
让我想想，我被无视了。

413
00:19:49.210 --> 00:19:54.590
I had Blitz's brother, Andy Blitz, and I created a part for him.
我让布里ッツ的兄弟安迪·布里ッツ来，我为他创作了一个角色。

414
00:19:54.870 --> 00:19:58.350
Well, I have to say, and Jenna and I have talked about this a lot, and we talked about
嗯，我必须说，珍娜和我经常讨论这个，当格雷格来的时候我们也讨论过

415
00:19:58.350 --> 00:20:05.430
this when Greg came on as well, that we loved that we got to be around the writers.
这件事，我们很喜欢能和编剧们在一起。

416
00:20:05.650 --> 00:20:07.890
We loved when we got to go up into the writer's room.
我们很喜欢去编剧室的时候。

417
00:20:08.030 --> 00:20:11.510
Sometimes we would shoot over in the warehouse and there was that back stairwell.
有时我们在仓库那边拍摄，那里有一个后楼梯。

418
00:20:11.790 --> 00:20:16.210
That went up where your kitchen was with your snacks, and we would come up and hang out.
通往你存放零食的厨房，我们会上去闲逛。

419
00:20:16.670 --> 00:20:20.090
And it was really fun for us to have you guys on set.
你们能在片场对我们来说真的很有趣。

420
00:20:20.310 --> 00:20:26.650
And it's hard for me to imagine other shows now without that creative collaboration and
现在我很难想象其他没有这种创意合作以及

421
00:20:26.650 --> 00:20:28.870
that feeling of safety and truSt.
那种安全感和信任感的剧集会是什么样子。

422
00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:32.150
And we've all worked on other shows where it is not the case.
我们都曾在其他并非如此的剧集里工作过。

423
00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:35.190
And it's something that I really cherish.
这是我非常珍惜的事情。

424
00:20:36.150 --> 00:20:37.250
Yeah, me too.
是的，我也是。

425
00:20:37.910 --> 00:20:38.770
Greg was right.
格雷格说得对。

426
00:20:40.270 --> 00:20:45.570
Breaking down that wall made us understand each other a lot better, and we all worked together.
打破那堵墙让我们更了解彼此，我们都一起合作。

427
00:20:45.770 --> 00:20:52.310
Well, speaking of having to team up, for this episode, the job, you teamed up with Mike
嗯，说到必须组队，对于这一集，“工作”，你和迈克·

428
00:20:52.310 --> 00:20:52.550
Schur.
舒尔合作了。

429
00:20:52.670 --> 00:20:54.450
You guys co-wrote this episode.
你们俩共同编剧了这一集。

430
00:20:54.650 --> 00:20:55.610
How did that work?
那是怎么运作的？

431
00:20:55.770 --> 00:21:00.870
I have kind of a memory of, you know, this was at the end of the season and a long season.
我有点记忆，你知道，这是在季末，一个漫长的季度。

432
00:21:00.990 --> 00:21:03.450
And a lot of episodes are written different ways.
而且很多剧集的创作方式都不同。

433
00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:10.410
So it wasn't that Mike and I went off into a room together and then came out with this
所以并不是我和迈克一起走进一个房间然后拿出了这集

434
00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:10.750
show.
节目。

435
00:21:11.010 --> 00:21:20.730
I think that we both were running the process of writing this episode together, you know,
我认为我们俩都在一起推进编写这一集的过程，你知道，

436
00:21:20.810 --> 00:21:26.270
and we would, we beat it all out with some writers would come in and out, but we would
我们会和一些进进出出的编剧一起把剧情推敲出来，但我们俩

437
00:21:26.270 --> 00:21:31.370
be the two people always there making sure, you know, the episode was what we wanted.
一直是那两个确保这一集就是我们想要的人。

438
00:21:31.370 --> 00:21:35.090
And then he would go take a scene, I would take a scene, or he would take a few writers
然后他会拿走一个场景，我拿走一个场景，或者他会带几个编剧

439
00:21:35.090 --> 00:21:37.070
to take a scene and I would do the same.
去处理一个场景，我也会这样做。

440
00:21:37.330 --> 00:21:39.570
I think that's basically how this one worked.
我想这基本上就是这一集的工作方式。

441
00:21:39.970 --> 00:21:45.190
It's funny that you mentioned working in groups like that, because I remember there were times
真有趣，你提到这样小组工作，因为我记得片场有几次

442
00:21:45.190 --> 00:21:50.730
on the set where Greg would call me off set.
格雷格会把我叫离片场。

443
00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:52.490
He would say, Jenna, are you in the scene?
他会说，珍娜，你在那个场景里吗？

444
00:21:52.750 --> 00:21:53.310
Are you in the scene?
你在那个场景里吗？

445
00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:53.530
Okay.
好的。

446
00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:56.650
I've got three writers talking about Jim and Pam.
我有三个编剧在讨论吉姆和帕姆。

447
00:21:56.810 --> 00:21:57.690
I want you to sit in on that.
我想让你去旁听一下。

448
00:22:01.370 --> 00:22:02.770
I would be like, oh, I can't wait.
我会想，哦，我等不及了。

449
00:22:02.970 --> 00:22:03.770
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

450
00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:05.850
And I mostly just listened.
而我大部分时间只是听着。

451
00:22:05.850 --> 00:22:07.550
And sometimes I would throw out ideas.
有时候我会提出一些点子。

452
00:22:08.110 --> 00:22:14.270
But that was so cool, because you guys would kind of divide up a script and like a group
但那真的很酷，因为你们会把剧本分一下，比如三个人一组

453
00:22:14.270 --> 00:22:16.590
of three people would go work on Dwight stuff.
去处理德怀特相关的戏份。

454
