然后大卫·华莱士就说，不好意思？

607
00:29:34.150 --> 00:29:34.990
Like just with a look.
就只是用那种眼神。

608
00:29:35.270 --> 00:29:35.320
Yeah.
对。

609
00:29:35.530 --> 00:29:36.890
And Michael's like, nope, nope.
然后迈克尔就说，没有，没有。

610
00:29:37.090 --> 00:29:37.270
Okay.
好吧。

611
00:29:37.450 --> 00:29:37.590
Okay.
好吧。

612
00:29:41.890 --> 00:29:46.070
We got one question from a fan, Paul, and I have to ask.
保罗，我们收到了一位粉丝的提问，我必须得问问。

613
00:29:46.230 --> 00:29:48.650
This is from Sarah McGinty and Zhu Yi Wang.
这是莎拉·麦金蒂和朱一王提出来的。

614
00:29:48.950 --> 00:29:53.650
They want to know why didn't Karen get the job at corporate?
他们想知道为什么凯伦没有得到总部的职位？

615
00:29:54.130 --> 00:30:00.010
Because you set up that one of the requirements for the job was sales experience of four years.
因为你们设定的职位要求之一是四年销售经验。

616
00:30:00.890 --> 00:30:05.250
But Ryan, we don't think has worked there for four years and he's never made a sale.
但瑞恩，我们觉得他没在那儿工作四年，而且他从来没卖出过东西。

617
00:30:06.570 --> 00:30:08.530
Why did David Wallace choose him?
为什么大卫·华莱士会选他？

618
00:30:08.970 --> 00:30:16.490
They want to know, did you do this so that you could get BJ off the set and into the writer's room so he could do his writing job?
他们想知道，你们这么做是不是为了让B·J离开片场去编剧室，好让他专心写剧本？

619
00:30:19.650 --> 00:30:20.870
No, probably the opposite.
不，可能恰恰相反。

620
00:30:21.090 --> 00:30:29.290
It was, I think we thought we would get a lot of fun comedy out of putting Ryan as Michael's boss for a while.
我觉得吧，我们觉得让瑞恩当一阵子迈克尔的上司，会产生很多好玩的喜剧效果。

621
00:30:29.770 --> 00:30:31.730
You know, he was the temp that came in.
你知道的，他是新来的临时工。

622
00:30:31.890 --> 00:30:38.290
He's clearly a really good bullshitter, but it's, but incompetent, you know.
他显然很会忽悠，但，但又很不称职，你知道的。

623
00:30:38.730 --> 00:30:40.090
And I think that's how he got it.
我觉得这就是他得到这个职位的原因。

624
00:30:40.190 --> 00:30:43.550
You know, I think we say he went to management school for a little.
你知道的，我们剧里说过他去上了个管理学校。

625
00:30:43.550 --> 00:30:45.490
He got an MBA, right?
他拿了MBA，对吧？

626
00:30:45.890 --> 00:30:47.150
That was one of the things.
那是其中一点。

627
00:30:47.150 --> 00:30:49.310
Yeah, so I'm not sure how he did that, maybe at night.
对，所以我不太确定他是怎么拿到的，可能是上夜校吧。

628
00:30:49.690 --> 00:30:59.250
But, I mean, the reasoning in the real world, you know, I could have been, he just really kind of dazzled David with the MBA and said all the right things.
但是，我是说，在现实世界里，我觉得原因可能是，他真的用MBA把大卫给镇住了，而且说得头头是道。

629
00:30:59.270 --> 00:31:01.850
So I could see, I could see it happening.
所以我能理解，我能想象这种事发生。

630
00:31:02.150 --> 00:31:07.290
But the real reason was like, you know, it was time for Karen to leave the show.
但真正的理由是，你知道的，凯伦是时候离开剧组了。

631
00:31:10.670 --> 00:31:13.210
And, you know, what we were doing with Jim and Pam.
还有，你知道的，我们对吉姆和帕姆的剧情安排。

632
00:31:14.150 --> 00:31:15.170
For season four.
为了第四季。

633
00:31:16.030 --> 00:31:20.090
And then, and then we thought it would be just a fun dynamic switch.
然后，然后我们觉得这会是一种很好玩的人物关系转变。

634
00:31:21.070 --> 00:31:21.930
I think it's a.
我觉得这。

635
00:31:21.930 --> 00:31:24.630
We were always looking for these pairings, you know, switch people up.
我们一直在寻找这种人物组合，你知道的，把大家调配一下。

636
00:31:24.810 --> 00:31:28.230
Who hasn't been together in a while, you know, so we have all your pictures up.
看看谁有好一阵子没搭过戏了，你知道的，所以我们把你们的照片都挂出来了。

637
00:31:28.370 --> 00:31:28.990
But what about you and you?
但是你和你就不好说了？

638
00:31:29.050 --> 00:31:30.370
Have we done a scene with Jim?
我们拍过吉姆的戏吗？

639
00:31:31.090 --> 00:31:39.430
What if you were his boss, you know, and you're always like, you know, status games and improv or power dynamics, you know, just switching them up.
要是你是他的上司呢，你知道的，你们总是喜欢搞什么地位博弈和即兴表演或者权力动态，你知道的，就是换着搭戏。

640
00:31:39.430 --> 00:31:40.550
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

641
00:31:40.670 --> 00:31:41.890
I just loved it so much.
我简直太喜欢了。

642
00:31:42.010 --> 00:31:47.130
I could really see why Ryan at corporate would just be, it's almost Shakespearean.
我真的能理解为什么总部的瑞恩会，这简直有点像莎士比亚的戏剧。

643
00:31:47.330 --> 00:31:56.730
You know, it's like Michael thinks of himself as the king and this like lowly, like peasant just, just went right past him, you know, on the food chain.
你知道的，就好像迈克尔自认为是国王，而这个低贱的、像农夫一样的人竟然，竟然就这么从他头顶上越过去了，你知道的，在食物链上。

644
00:31:56.730 --> 00:32:06.930
And I love that he was like, give me a coffee, you know, and then, and then now, now Ryan just jumped right over him and it's going to be at corporate.
我喜欢他之前说的那句，给我倒杯咖啡，你知道的，然后，现在，现在瑞恩直接跳到他头上去了，而且还要去总部高就。

645
00:32:06.930 --> 00:32:16.110
And just the way he says goodbye to Kelly, he's like cold, he's cold hearted, but you can see that there's, there's going to be some fun there.
还有他跟凯利道别的方式，他就像个冷血动物，冷酷无情，但你能看出，这其中会有很多好玩的看点。

646
00:32:16.570 --> 00:32:16.810
Yeah.
对。

647
00:32:17.210 --> 00:32:17.670
Yeah.
对。

648
00:32:17.910 --> 00:32:18.910
He's like, we're done.
他就好像在说，我们结束了。

649
00:32:19.110 --> 00:32:19.310
Yeah.
对。

650
00:32:19.610 --> 00:32:27.210
Paul, is there anything when you look back and you think to yourself, I wish we had done this scene?
保罗，有没有哪件事当你回想起来时，会心想，我真希望当时拍了这场戏？

651
00:32:27.210 --> 00:32:37.390
Because I remember there was a card on the writer's room wall for years and years and years that never got made and it haunts me and it said double date.
因为我记得编剧室的墙上贴着一张卡片，好多年好多年一直都没有拍成，它一直萦绕在我的心头，上面写着双人约会。

652
00:32:37.890 --> 00:32:41.870
And it was going to be a double date with Jim and Pam and Dwight and Angela.
原本设想的是吉姆和帕姆，还有德怀特和安吉拉的双人约会。

653
00:32:42.710 --> 00:32:46.870
And I always wish we had seen that double date.
我一直很遗憾我们没能看到那场双人约会。

654
00:32:46.870 --> 00:32:55.790
And I even remember being in the writer's room and hearing you guys try to justify why Jim and Pam would agree to go on a double date with Dwight and Angela.
我甚至记得自己当时在编剧室里，听你们大家试图去解释，为什么吉姆和帕姆会同意跟德怀特和安吉拉去双人约会。

655
00:32:56.410 --> 00:32:58.910
How could you make that happen?
你们怎么能让那种事发生呢？

656
00:32:58.910 --> 00:33:01.930
Or vice versa, how, why, why would Angela ever attend?
或者反过来，安吉拉怎么会、为什么会去参加呢？

657
00:33:02.550 --> 00:33:08.030
And I think dinner party was sort of that, right?
我觉得《晚宴》那一集某种程度上就是那样的吧？

658
00:33:08.230 --> 00:33:11.750
We all did go out on our kind of double, triple date there.
我们大家确实都在那里进行了一场双人、三人约会。

659
00:33:12.430 --> 00:33:15.910
Quadruple date, really, with, since Dwight brought his babysitter.
其实算是四人约会，因为德怀特把他的保姆也带上了。

660
00:33:15.910 --> 00:33:20.430
Were there any cards that you remember that you had to leave on the wall?
你还记得有什么卡片是你不得不留在墙上的吗？

661
00:33:20.610 --> 00:33:21.850
You had to leave them behind?
你不得不把它们留在那里？

662
00:33:22.610 --> 00:33:24.390
I'm absolutely sure there were.
我百分之百确定是有的。

663
00:33:24.870 --> 00:33:26.030
Double date would have been fun.
双人约会本来会很有趣的。

664
00:33:26.310 --> 00:33:28.530
Sometimes it's finding the killer joke.
有时候关键在于找到那个绝妙的笑点。

665
00:33:28.770 --> 00:33:35.170
Like we maybe, you know, we should have just been pitching on what is the hysterical thing that's going to happen.
就像我们可能，你知道的，我们本该去构思接下来要发生的那个爆笑情节是什么。

666
00:33:35.390 --> 00:33:39.010
Because then we find that and you're like, oh, we'll do whatever it takes to justify it.
因为一旦我们找到了，你就会觉得，噢，我们愿意付出任何代价来让它合情合理。

667
00:33:40.430 --> 00:33:43.410
Paul, thank you so much for coming on Office Ladies.
保罗，非常感谢你来到《办公室女士》节目。

668
00:33:43.630 --> 00:33:44.950
We were just thrilled to have you.
你能来我们真是太兴奋了。

669
00:33:45.390 --> 00:33:46.630
Thanks for having me on.
谢谢邀请我来。

670
00:33:46.810 --> 00:33:47.030
Yeah.
好。

671
00:33:47.690 --> 00:33:48.790
Well, thanks, Paul.
好的，谢谢你，保罗。

672
00:33:48.930 --> 00:33:50.250
It was really good to see you.
很高兴见到你。

673
00:33:50.730 --> 00:33:54.550
And I hope that we can have another get together really soon.
希望我们很快能再次聚聚。

674
00:33:55.050 --> 00:33:55.790
I hope so, too.
我也希望如此。

675
00:33:55.890 --> 00:33:56.370
All right, Paul.
好的，保罗。

676
00:33:56.510 --> 00:33:56.770
Hugs.
一个拥抱。

677
00:33:56.770 --> 00:33:56.890
All right.
好的。

678
00:33:57.050 --> 00:33:57.730
Take care, guys.
保重，各位。

679
00:33:57.830 --> 00:33:58.450
Bye, Paul.
再见，保罗。

680
00:33:58.930 --> 00:33:59.330
Bye.
再见。

681
00:34:00.270 --> 00:34:00.590
Bye.
再见。

682
00:34:03.610 --> 00:34:05.450
Well, that was just too much fun.
真是太有意思了。

683
00:34:05.710 --> 00:34:08.090
I love it when we have writers on the show.
我太喜欢节目里有编剧来做客了。

684
00:34:08.250 --> 00:34:09.510
And Paul is the writer-actor.
而且保罗既是编剧又是演员。

685
00:34:09.710 --> 00:34:11.570
He brings such a cool perspective.
他带来了非常酷的视角。

686
00:34:11.570 --> 00:34:12.250
Right, Jenna?
对吧，珍娜？

687
00:34:12.730 --> 00:34:13.070
Yeah.
对。

688
00:34:13.070 --> 00:34:15.350
Well, listen, we want to give Paul a shout-out here.
听着，我们要在这里向保罗致敬一下。

689
00:34:15.450 --> 00:34:19.170
He has a really funny new project coming out spring of 2021.
他有一个非常搞笑的新项目将在2021年春季推出。

690
00:34:19.650 --> 00:34:21.070
It's going to be on Audible.
它将在Audible上发布。

691
00:34:21.490 --> 00:34:23.210
And it's a show called Captain.
这是一档名叫《船长》的节目。

692
00:34:23.530 --> 00:34:25.670
He said it's like an old-time radio show.
他说这就像是一个老式的广播剧。

693
00:34:25.850 --> 00:34:28.610
And it's a sci-fi, but it's anti-sci-fi.
这是一部科幻作品，但又是反科幻的。

694
00:34:28.830 --> 00:34:30.290
I love this description.
我很喜欢这个描述。

695
00:34:30.610 --> 00:34:31.690
It's anti-sci-fi.
它是反科幻的。

696
00:34:31.830 --> 00:34:32.750
Jenna's like, I'm on board.
珍娜的反应就像是，我加入了。

697
00:34:32.750 --> 00:34:40.250
It has Will Forte, John Malkovich, Rainn Wilson, Adam Scott, Wyatt Cenac, Gillian Jacobs, lots
里面有威尔·福特、约翰·马尔科维奇、雷恩·威尔森、亚当·斯科特、怀亚特·西纳克、吉莉安·雅各布斯，还有很多

698
00:34:40.250 --> 00:34:41.050
of funny folks.
搞笑的大咖。

699
00:34:41.250 --> 00:34:43.370
Be looking for it spring 2021.
请在2021年春季关注它。

700
00:34:43.790 --> 00:34:45.090
Captain on Audible.
Audible上的《船长》。

701
00:34:45.430 --> 00:34:46.070
Yeah.
是啊。

702
00:34:46.270 --> 00:34:52.230
He said it's like they're all out in space, but there's nothing sci-fi happening to them,
他说这就像他们都在太空中一样，但他们身上并没有发生任何科幻的事情，

703
00:34:52.310 --> 00:34:55.210
which I just thought was so funny.
我只是觉得这太搞笑了。

704
00:34:56.010 --> 00:34:57.570
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

705
00:34:57.770 --> 00:34:58.890
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

706
00:34:58.890 --> 00:35:03.450
Well, listen, guys, we will take a break, and then when we come back, we will start
好了，听着，伙计们，我们要休息一下，然后等我们回来，我们就开始

707
00:35:03.450 --> 00:35:05.190
breaking down the job.
剖析这项工作。

708
00:35:16.510 --> 00:35:17.030
All right.
好的。

709
00:35:17.030 --> 00:35:24.350
So this episode opens with Michael at corporate for his interview, which is tomorrow.
所以这一集一开场就是迈克尔去总公司面试，面试是明天。

710
00:35:25.030 --> 00:35:25.150
Yeah.
是啊。

711
00:35:25.210 --> 00:35:28.510
He got the day wrong, and now he's got to cover his butt.
他记错日子了，现在他得想办法掩盖过去。

712
00:35:28.790 --> 00:35:28.910
Yeah.
是啊。

713
00:35:28.950 --> 00:35:32.230
He's trying to save it, and he does a horrible job.
他在试图挽回，结果搞得一团糟。

714
00:35:32.390 --> 00:35:32.570
Yeah.
是啊。

715
00:35:32.910 --> 00:35:34.950
And I wanted to point out something.
我想指出一件事。

716
00:35:35.210 --> 00:35:37.810
While him and David Wallace are talking, I looked at reception.
当他和大卫·华莱士在说话时，我看了看前台。

717
00:35:38.510 --> 00:35:39.510
No plants.
没有植物。

718
00:35:39.770 --> 00:35:40.850
At reception corporate.
总公司的前台。

719
00:35:41.210 --> 00:35:42.610
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

720
00:35:42.690 --> 00:35:46.790
Now you're tracking the plants at corporate reception.
现在你连总公司前台的植物都开始注意了。

721
00:35:47.070 --> 00:35:47.750
What's wrong with me?
我这是怎么了？

722
00:35:48.030 --> 00:35:55.210
But at 33 seconds, there is a really good shot of some dried brown sticks in the back.
但在第33秒时，有一个非常清晰的特写，背景里有一些干枯的褐色枝条。

723
00:35:55.390 --> 00:35:56.270
It's like sticks.
就像是棍子。

724
00:35:56.550 --> 00:35:58.770
Big, tall looking sticks.
又大又高的棍子。

725
00:35:59.130 --> 00:36:00.750
I mean, they're not really alive, right?
我是说，它们其实不是活的，对吧？

726
00:36:00.870 --> 00:36:02.150
This is some kind of decor.
这是某种装饰。

727
00:36:02.630 --> 00:36:06.730
Well, clearly, the receptionist at corporate is doing something right.
很显然，总公司的前台小姐做得很对。

728
00:36:06.870 --> 00:36:08.150
She doesn't have to keep any plants alive.
她不用费心让任何植物保持活着。

729
00:36:08.150 --> 00:36:09.990
She's just got a jar with sticks.
她只有一个插着树枝的罐子。

730
00:36:10.290 --> 00:36:10.970
I like it.
我喜欢。

731
00:36:11.270 --> 00:36:12.330
Pam could learn something.
帕姆可以学着点。

732
00:36:12.710 --> 00:36:14.410
We should get into the episode.
我们该进入正片了。

733
00:36:15.130 --> 00:36:21.070
So Jim arrives to work, and Jenna, Jim has a new haircut.
吉姆来上班了，珍娜，吉姆换了个新发型。

734
00:36:21.650 --> 00:36:22.350
He does.
确实。

735
00:36:22.550 --> 00:36:24.030
Meredith thinks it looks sexy.
梅雷迪思觉得这看起来很性感。

736
00:36:24.250 --> 00:36:24.830
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

737
00:36:25.490 --> 00:36:27.730
And Kevin thinks he could look worse.
凯文觉得他其实可以更难看一点。

738
00:36:28.090 --> 00:36:31.090
Andy immediately says, you're no longer big tuna.
安迪立刻说，你不再是大金枪鱼了。

739
00:36:31.090 --> 00:36:32.030
You're big haircut.
你是大发型。

740
00:36:32.030 --> 00:36:35.030
Well, we got a lot of fan questions about this, Angela.
安吉拉，我们收到了很多关于这的粉丝提问。

741
00:36:35.330 --> 00:36:42.610
Samantha Patino, Kayla O, Katie Nolder, Jess Kahn, Natalie Payne, and many others wrote in to ask,
萨曼莎·帕蒂尼、凯拉·O、凯蒂·诺尔德、杰斯·卡恩、娜塔莉·佩恩以及许多其他人写信来问，

742
00:36:42.850 --> 00:36:48.510
was Jim's haircut a writer choice, or was there another reason he got the haircut?
吉姆的发型是编剧的选择，还是有其他原因？

743
00:36:48.730 --> 00:36:49.630
It was both.
两者皆有。

744
00:36:49.930 --> 00:36:50.910
It was both.
两者皆有。

745
00:36:51.110 --> 00:36:51.550
It was both.
两者皆有。

746
00:36:51.550 --> 00:36:55.890
It was in the script, but it had to be in the script because John got a haircut.
剧本里写了，但必须写进剧本是因为约翰剪了头发。

747
00:36:55.890 --> 00:37:05.130
Well, John was doing a movie with George Clooney and Renee Zellweger called Leatherheads, and it was set in a different time, and so he had shorter hair.
约翰当时在和乔治·克鲁尼以及芮妮·齐薇格拍一部名为《皮革heads》的电影，故事背景设定在不同的年代，所以他的头发剪短了。

748
00:37:05.350 --> 00:37:10.170
But it worked out perfect for the story because I think it's great that Karen's like, you need a haircut.
但这跟剧情配合得完美无瑕，因为我觉得凯伦说“你需要理发”这一点太棒了，

749
00:37:10.170 --> 00:37:16.350
You're going to interview for corporate, and Jim did kind of have this shaggy hair, you know?
你要去总公司面试，而且吉姆的头发确实有点蓬乱，你知道吗？

750
00:37:16.810 --> 00:37:20.050
So I liked that Karen, as the girlfriend, was like, you got to clean it up.
所以我很喜欢凯伦作为女朋友说的那句，你得修剪一下了。

751
00:37:20.450 --> 00:37:29.550
But there were a few episodes this season, some of you guys have asked, that as John's hair was sort of transitioning back from that haircut of the movie, that he did wear a wig.
不过这季有几集，正如你们有些人问过的，因为约翰的头发当时正在从拍电影的那个发型慢慢留回长发，所以他确实戴过假发。

752
00:37:29.910 --> 00:37:30.310
Yes.
对。

753
00:37:30.670 --> 00:37:33.950
And we have not talked about that, which is so crazy to me.
而且我们之前居然没聊过这个，我觉得太疯狂了。

754
00:37:33.950 --> 00:37:41.990
But yeah, after he got the super short haircut for the movie, he came back to the office, and he had to wear a wig for a while where his hair grew out.
对啊，他为了拍电影剪了超短发之后，回到了办公室，在头发长出来的这段时间里，他不得不戴了一段时间的假发。

755
00:37:42.150 --> 00:37:48.630
And then finally, for this episode, I think they felt like it had grown out enough that it looked like a more modern-day haircut.
然后最后到了这一集，我想他们觉得头发长得差不多了，看起来更像是个现代的发型了。

756
00:37:48.870 --> 00:37:51.930
So this is John's real hair, folks.
所以各位，这是约翰真正的头发。

757
00:37:52.130 --> 00:37:52.430
Yes.
对。

758
00:37:52.590 --> 00:37:53.010
Yes.
对。

759
00:37:53.270 --> 00:38:00.330
You guys, I went to the Leatherheads premiere, and I met John's family, and I could not believe it.
天哪，我去了《爱情达阵》的首映礼，我还见到了约翰的家人，我简直不敢相信。

760
00:38:00.330 --> 00:38:04.830
I walked up to the group of them, and John was like, hey, guys, this is my friend Angela.
我朝他们那群人走过去，约翰就说，嘿，大家，这是我的朋友安杰拉。

761
00:38:05.030 --> 00:38:07.730
And they turned around, and they were the tallest people.
然后他们转过身来，他们真的是最高大的人。

762
00:38:08.330 --> 00:38:10.650
John is the shortest of his brothers, guys.
各位，约翰是他兄弟中最矮的一个。

763
00:38:11.210 --> 00:38:13.370
And he's like 6'3".
而他身高有六英尺三英寸。

764
00:38:13.370 --> 00:38:14.470
He's 6'3".
他有六英尺三英寸高。

765
00:38:14.470 --> 00:38:15.470
He's the shorteSt.
他是最矮的。

766
00:38:15.770 --> 00:38:17.190
I was like, oh, my gosh.
当时我就想，哦，天哪。

767
00:38:17.270 --> 00:38:19.610
It was like we're from two different planets.
感觉就像我们来自两个不同的星球。

768
00:38:19.790 --> 00:38:23.810
But they were so lovely, and that was so fun to be able to go support him like that.
但他们真的非常可爱，能去那样支持他真的太有趣了。

769
00:38:24.630 --> 00:38:24.970
Yeah.
是的。

770
00:38:25.290 --> 00:38:28.550
Yeah, that was really cool when he was shooting that movie, actually.
是的，其实当他在拍那部电影的时候，真的很酷。

771
00:38:28.550 --> 00:38:34.710
We would get excited for each other when we would get these jobs, and we'd be like, tell us all about it.
当我们接到这些工作时，我们会为彼此感到兴奋，我们会说，快跟我们讲讲所有细节。

772
00:38:34.850 --> 00:38:35.310
I know.
我知道。

773
00:38:35.510 --> 00:38:37.830
I was like, George Clooney, come on.
我就觉得，乔治·克鲁尼，拜托。

774
00:38:38.550 --> 00:38:38.890
No.
不是的。

775
00:38:39.210 --> 00:38:42.110
I wanted to point out something, though, with his talking head.
不过，我想指出关于他单人访谈的一个细节。

776
00:38:42.330 --> 00:38:45.830
You know, he says that Karen suggested he get a haircut for his interview.
你知道的，他说凯伦建议他为面试剪个头发。

777
00:38:46.190 --> 00:38:49.350
And Jenna, this is a major girlfriend moment.
珍娜，这绝对是一个非常重大的女友高光时刻。

778
00:38:49.610 --> 00:38:53.490
I mean, A, it shows that Jim is actually really listening to Karen.
我是说，首先，这表明吉姆其实真的把凯伦的话听进去了。

779
00:38:53.490 --> 00:39:02.170
You know, changing your look, especially when you've had the same haircut or same look for years and years, that's a big deal.
你知道的，改变你的外表，特别是当你多年来一直保持同一个发型或同样的造型时，这可是一件大事。

780
00:39:02.670 --> 00:39:07.150
And so he took her advice, and I thought, oh, wow, their relationship's really solid.
所以他听取了她的建议，当时我想，哦，哇，他们的关系真的很稳固。

781
00:39:07.330 --> 00:39:08.290
Like, I was believing it.
就像，我当时真的相信了。

782
00:39:08.370 --> 00:39:09.670
I'm like, wow, Jim's all in.
我心想，哇，吉姆是完全投入了。

783
00:39:09.970 --> 00:39:14.910
And then I thought it also shows that he really wants to get the job.
然后我想，这也表明他真的很想得到这份工作。

784
00:39:14.910 --> 00:39:20.370
Well, in this episode, there are going to be a ton of Mr. X.
好吧，在这集里，会有大量的X先生。

785
00:39:20.590 --> 00:39:25.510
We do not show our hand for what the end of this is going to be at all.
我们一点也没有提前透露这件事最后会怎样。

786
00:39:25.650 --> 00:39:33.150
And coming back from Beach Games, it was like, what is going to be the repercussion of Pam's confession on the beach?
从《海滩游戏》回来后，大家都在想，帕姆在海滩上的表白会带来什么后果？

787
00:39:33.670 --> 00:39:42.410
And so to open this episode with Jim and Karen stronger than ever, Pam is like, listen, it went great.
所以这集一开场就是吉姆和凯伦比以往任何时候都更恩爱，而帕姆则一副，听着，一切都挺好的样子。

788
00:39:42.730 --> 00:39:43.690
It was fine.
一切都很好。

789
00:39:43.890 --> 00:39:49.950
She has that whole talking head where she's like, I know it only took me three years to summon the courage to tell Jim my feelings.
她有一段很长的单人访谈，里面大概是说，我知道我花了三年时间才鼓起勇气把内心的感受告诉吉姆。

790
00:39:49.970 --> 00:39:52.150
But, you know, I'm glad I did it.
但是，你知道的，我很高兴我这么做了。

791
00:39:52.270 --> 00:39:52.950
Now it's over.
现在事情已经结束了。

792
00:39:53.090 --> 00:39:54.270
We're all moving on.
我们都要向前看了。

793
00:39:54.570 --> 00:39:56.230
That's how we open this episode.
这就是我们这一集的开场方式。

794
00:39:56.590 --> 00:39:57.610
We're all moving on.
我们都要向前看了。

795
00:39:57.910 --> 00:39:58.670
Jim has a haircut.
吉姆剪了头发。

796
00:39:59.070 --> 00:40:00.390
He likes his girlfriend's advice.
他很听女友的建议。

797
00:40:00.390 --> 00:40:08.650
I was really, I don't even know the word, like in awe maybe of Pam's talking head about how she was like, I have no regrets.
我真的是，我都不知道该用什么词，也许是对帕姆的单人访谈感到敬畏吧，她当时说，我毫无遗憾。

798
00:40:08.650 --> 00:40:09.830
It needed to be said.
这事必须说出来。

799
00:40:09.950 --> 00:40:12.990
And I said it because I would have been horrified.
我把它说出来了，因为否则我会吓坏的。

800
00:40:13.350 --> 00:40:15.830
I would have been so embarrassed.
我会觉得太尴尬了。

801
00:40:15.830 --> 00:40:20.370
Like that I have this huge, like emotional speech in front of all of my coworkers.
就像我在所有同事面前发表了一场巨大的、充满情绪的演讲一样。

802
00:40:20.610 --> 00:40:26.290
But then you got to show up to work the next day with everyone in the bright fluorescent light.
但接着你第二天就得在明亮的荧光灯下和大家一起去上班。

803
00:40:28.150 --> 00:40:28.670
Yeah.
对啊。

804
00:40:28.670 --> 00:40:30.470
Well, they do tease her a little bit.
嗯，他们确实有点逗她。

805
00:40:30.610 --> 00:40:32.390
There are a bunch of deleted scenes.
有很多删减片段。

806
00:40:32.550 --> 00:40:33.170
There's a runner.
有个贯穿全剧的笑点。

807
00:40:33.190 --> 00:40:34.450
And we'll see one later.
我们稍后会看到一个。

808
00:40:34.610 --> 00:40:37.010
But you do get made fun of a little bit.
但你确实会被取笑一点点。

809
00:40:37.110 --> 00:40:38.610
But lovingly by everyone.
不过大家都是带着爱意的。

810
00:40:39.390 --> 00:40:39.750
Yes.
没错。

811
00:40:40.090 --> 00:40:43.370
Well, next up, Michael is in his office.
那么，接下来，迈克尔在办公室里。

812
00:40:43.410 --> 00:40:45.050
He calls Dwight in.
他把德怀特叫了进去。

813
00:40:45.430 --> 00:40:48.970
And he explains, it's time for me to name my successor.
他解释说，是时候让我指定继承人了。

814
00:40:49.230 --> 00:40:51.010
He hands Dwight an envelope.
他递给德怀特一个信封。

815
00:40:51.010 --> 00:40:51.810
Yes.
是的。

816
00:40:52.110 --> 00:40:58.950
And inside, there is a written note from Michael that says, Dwight, congratulations, A-Wipe.
里面是迈克尔写的一张便条，上面写着：德怀特，恭喜你，屁眼擦。

817
00:40:59.250 --> 00:41:00.650
Don't screw the pooch.
别搞砸了。

818
00:41:02.310 --> 00:41:05.250
And Dwight begins sobbing.
然后德怀特开始啜泣。

819
00:41:05.330 --> 00:41:06.630
It brings Dwight to sobbing.
这让德怀特哭了起来。

820
00:41:06.750 --> 00:41:07.010
Sobbing.
啜泣。

821
00:41:07.010 --> 00:41:07.230
Sobbing.
啜泣。

822
00:41:07.710 --> 00:41:15.650
I listened to the DVD commentary, and they said in the commentary that Rain as Dwight went on and on, so long sobbing.
我听了DVD的评论音轨，他们在评论音轨里说雷恩饰演的德怀特一直在哭，哭了超级久。

823
00:41:15.770 --> 00:41:17.670
They just let him just sob.
他们就让他一直哭。

824
00:41:17.830 --> 00:41:20.190
Ken Coapis just let him go and let him go.
肯·科皮斯就一直让他哭个不停。

825
00:41:20.830 --> 00:41:23.150
And Ken said it went on for so long.
肯说这持续了太久。

826
00:41:23.290 --> 00:41:24.630
And Steve started saying, you know what?
然后史蒂夫开始说，你知道吗？

827
00:41:24.630 --> 00:41:25.330
Just forget it.
算了吧。

828
00:41:25.430 --> 00:41:26.710
Give me the letter back.
把信还给我。

829
00:41:26.930 --> 00:41:28.270
I take it back.
我收回这话。

830
00:41:29.950 --> 00:41:35.430
Well, we had a fan catch in this scene, which is really delightful, Angela.
嗯，我们在这一场戏里发现了一个粉丝彩蛋，真的很有趣，安吉拉。

831
00:41:35.770 --> 00:41:41.950
Christina Juarez and John Sperry wrote in to say, in Michael's office, when he hands Dwight the letter,
克里斯蒂娜·华雷斯和约翰·斯佩里写信说，在迈克尔的办公室里，当他把信递给德怀特时，

832
00:41:42.210 --> 00:41:48.590
you can see an outlet on the wall behind Michael, and it is upside down.
你能看到迈克尔身后墙上的一个插座，它是倒着装的。

833
00:41:49.150 --> 00:41:50.690
What is going on here?
这到底是怎么回事？

834
00:41:51.710 --> 00:41:53.190
Oh, my God, Angela.
哦，天哪，安吉拉。

835
00:41:53.470 --> 00:41:54.150
It is.
真的是这样。

836
00:41:54.150 --> 00:41:58.310
It is right around 3 minutes, 11 seconds by the coat rack behind Michael.
就在大约3分11秒，在迈克尔身后的衣帽架旁。

837
00:41:59.210 --> 00:42:01.770
It's an upside down electrical outlet.
那是一个倒过来的电源插座。

838
00:42:01.950 --> 00:42:05.930
Like, the little hole part is on the top, and then the two lines are underneath it.
就是，小圆孔部分在上面，然后两个插孔在下面。

839
00:42:06.090 --> 00:42:14.710
I know what an upside down outlet would look like, but thank you for walking us through it.
我知道倒过来的插座长什么样，不过谢谢你给我们详细描述一遍。

840
00:42:14.870 --> 00:42:17.590
Well, if you want to see one, go to 3 minutes and 11 seconds.
嗯，如果你想看一个，就去看3分11秒。

841
00:42:17.870 --> 00:42:18.850
Well, that's a great catch.
嗯，真是个了不起的发现。

842
00:42:18.970 --> 00:42:19.530
You guys know.
你们懂的。

843
00:42:19.630 --> 00:42:20.830
I will go back and look for it.
我会回去找找看的。

844
00:42:21.770 --> 00:42:22.790
Here's something, Angela.
有个事儿，安吉拉。

845
00:42:22.790 --> 00:42:25.250
Of course, we know that that outlet didn't really work.
当然，我们知道那个插座其实不能用。

846
00:42:25.830 --> 00:42:30.510
It was just, you know, a fake outlet cover, but it did get me wondering.
那只是个假插座盖，你知道的，但这确实让我好奇起来。

847
00:42:32.090 --> 00:42:35.430
So, I went to the website, familyhandyman.com.
所以我上了网站，familyhandyman.com。

848
00:42:35.550 --> 00:42:36.430
Oh, Lord.
噢，天哪。

849
00:42:36.950 --> 00:42:42.330
And it says that there is actually no right way to install an outlet.
上面说其实安装插座并没有所谓的正确方向。

850
00:42:43.310 --> 00:42:47.030
You can install it, quote, upside down.
你可以把它安装成，引用原话，“倒装”。

851
00:42:47.030 --> 00:42:48.330
You can install it sideways.
你可以把它横着装。

852
00:42:48.330 --> 00:42:51.470
It will not affect how the outlet works.
这不会影响插座的使用。

853
00:42:51.470 --> 00:42:53.590
It actually said, quote, it's up to you.
它上面原话是这么写的，由你决定。

854
00:42:53.950 --> 00:42:59.430
There's no standard electrical outlet orientation, so there's really no such thing as an upside down outlet.
标准电气插座没有固定的方向，所以根本没有插座装反了这一说。

855
00:42:59.850 --> 00:43:01.170
Well, that makes sense.
嗯，这倒也合理。

856
00:43:02.190 --> 00:43:03.370
It does make sense.
确实挺合理的。

857
00:43:03.370 --> 00:43:04.270
I found it interesting.
我觉得这挺有意思的。

858
00:43:04.270 --> 00:43:08.310
I feel like my dad, I definitely need to tell my dad about familyhandyman.com.
我感觉自己像我爸，我绝对得把我爸推荐给 familyhandyman.com。

859
00:43:08.310 --> 00:43:10.010
Oh, your dad will love it.
噢，你爸一定会喜欢的。

860
00:43:10.510 --> 00:43:23.670
I also want to say, before we move on, that I noticed that there are also two light switches in the middle of Michael's wall underneath a giant framed picture.
我还想说，在我们继续之前，我注意到迈克尔的墙中央、一个巨大的有框画下面，也有两个电灯开关。

861
00:43:24.150 --> 00:43:25.510
Now, that is odd.
这就很奇怪了。

862
00:43:25.810 --> 00:43:29.270
Why would you put your light switches there?
为什么要把电灯开关装在那儿呢？

863
00:43:30.230 --> 00:43:34.610
I guess it's because when you walk in the door, he has, like, glass, so you can't.
我想可能是因为他一进门那里有玻璃什么的，所以不行。

864
00:43:35.050 --> 00:43:38.170
But he has to walk real far into his office to turn on the lights.
但他得走进办公室很远才能开灯。

865
00:43:38.590 --> 00:43:39.270
I'm just saying.
我只是随口说说。

866
00:43:39.270 --> 00:43:39.730
Well, you know what?
好吧，你知道吗？

867
00:43:39.790 --> 00:43:43.690
He never has to do it because Dwight gets there early and sets up his office for him.
他根本不用自己开，因为德怀特去得很早，会帮他把办公室收拾妥当。

868
00:43:44.130 --> 00:43:44.310
Yeah.
对啊。

869
00:43:44.870 --> 00:43:47.070
Michael doesn't even know where those light switches are.
迈克尔甚至都不知道那些开关在哪。

870
00:43:47.250 --> 00:43:48.450
He's never had to turn them on.
他从来没开过灯。

871
00:43:48.450 --> 00:43:50.950
Well, they're right there under the picture.
好吧，它们就在那幅画底下。

872
00:43:52.110 --> 00:43:53.230
You know what, Angela?
你知道吗，安吉拉？

873
00:43:53.430 --> 00:43:54.370
You spot plants.
你善于发现绿植。

874
00:43:54.510 --> 00:43:56.290
I'm going to be on the lookout for outlets.
我以后可得留意插座了。

875
00:43:56.670 --> 00:43:59.030
Well, between the two of us, lookout world.
咱们俩联手，世界可得小心了。

876
00:43:59.370 --> 00:44:00.170
That's right.
没错。

877
00:44:00.530 --> 00:44:05.050
Well, next up, the scene between Pam and Karen.
好了，接下来是帕姆和凯伦的对手戏。

878
00:44:05.410 --> 00:44:06.490
Oh, my gosh.
噢，天哪。

879
00:44:06.630 --> 00:44:16.430
I thought Rashida did such an amazing job because she had to react to so many things as Karen.
我觉得拉什达演得太棒了，因为作为凯伦，她得对很多事情作出反应。

880
00:44:16.430 --> 00:44:21.550
First of all, she's graciously, I think, trying to let Pam off the hook.
首先，我觉得她表现得很体贴，试图给帕姆一个台阶下。

881
00:44:21.710 --> 00:44:22.390
She's like, you know what?
她就像是在说，你知道吗？

882
00:44:22.710 --> 00:44:23.550
It happens.
这很正常。

883
00:44:23.690 --> 00:44:24.910
Sometimes we just have those moments.
有时候我们就是会遇到那种时刻。

884
00:44:25.010 --> 00:44:26.010
We say things we don't mean.
我们会说出言不由衷的话。

885
00:44:26.210 --> 00:44:28.210
And then Pam is like, oh, no, I meant it.
然后帕姆却说，哦，不，我是认真的。

886
00:44:28.330 --> 00:44:29.850
I've thought about it a long time.
我想了很久了。

887
00:44:30.350 --> 00:44:36.210
And Karen, the look that comes over her face, she's like, oh, that's how it is.
接着凯伦脸上露出的表情仿佛在说，哦，原来是这样。

888
00:44:37.250 --> 00:44:37.690
Yeah.
对啊。

889
00:44:38.310 --> 00:44:43.250
And then she has her talking head where she's like, Pam is kind of a bitch.
然后她有一段面对镜头的独白，大意是帕姆有点婊。

890
00:44:43.410 --> 00:44:43.830
Yeah.
对。

891
00:44:44.990 --> 00:44:45.430
Yeah.
