1039
00:52:09.130 --> 00:52:14.650
It is at blog.nbc.com backslash Creed Thoughts.
网址是 blog.nbc.com 反斜杠 Creed Thoughts。

1040
00:52:15.110 --> 00:52:16.370
I looked at it.
我看过了。

1041
00:52:17.370 --> 00:52:19.490
There are so many amazing things.
里面有太多惊人的内容了。

1042
00:52:20.730 --> 00:52:28.970
He has a whole story on there about how he stayed late one night at the office and he found a squirrel in Michael's safe.
他在上面写了个完整的故事，说他有一天晚上在办公室加班到很晚，在迈克尔的保险箱里发现了一只松鼠。

1043
00:52:29.650 --> 00:52:30.830
That's one of the stories.
这是其中一个故事。

1044
00:52:31.010 --> 00:52:31.250
What?
什么？

1045
00:52:31.870 --> 00:52:32.350
Yes.
对。

1046
00:52:32.750 --> 00:52:33.230
Yes.
没错。

1047
00:52:33.350 --> 00:52:40.670
He says he's so glad that he figured out the combination of Michael's safe because it ended up saving a squirrel's life.
他说他很高兴自己琢磨出了迈克尔保险箱的密码，因为这最终救了松鼠一命。

1048
00:52:41.370 --> 00:52:44.230
He would like to know why Michael put a squirrel in his safe.
他很想知道为什么迈克尔要把松鼠放进保险箱里。

1049
00:52:44.790 --> 00:52:46.230
That's one of his entries.
这是他的其中一篇博文。

1050
00:52:46.850 --> 00:52:49.850
Creed, did you really put it in there and then you forgot about it?
克里德，该不会真的是你放进去然后自己忘了吧？

1051
00:52:50.610 --> 00:52:51.570
It's possible.
有可能。

1052
00:52:51.810 --> 00:52:52.250
It's possible.
有可能。

1053
00:52:53.150 --> 00:52:54.350
But you can check it out.
不过你可以去查证一下。

1054
00:52:54.510 --> 00:52:54.970
It's still there.
它还在那儿。

1055
00:52:55.350 --> 00:52:56.370
That's so fun.
太有趣了。

1056
00:52:56.530 --> 00:52:57.350
That's so fun.
太有趣了。

1057
00:52:57.530 --> 00:52:59.050
I didn't know it was still active.
我不知道它还在运作。

1058
00:52:59.370 --> 00:53:00.330
That's so fun.
太有趣了。

1059
00:53:00.550 --> 00:53:08.110
Well, now Michael visits the accounting department and he's talking about his new job and how he's already sold his condo.
嗯，现在迈克尔来到会计部门，谈论他的新工作以及他是如何已经卖掉公寓的。

1060
00:53:08.490 --> 00:53:11.530
And they're like, whoa, whoa, whoa.
然后他们就觉得，等等，等等，等等。

1061
00:53:11.890 --> 00:53:12.170
What?
什么？

1062
00:53:13.730 --> 00:53:15.310
And I love this scene.
我很喜欢这个场景。

1063
00:53:15.470 --> 00:53:17.850
I remembered when we were doing the scene.
我记得我们拍这场戏的时候。

1064
00:53:18.030 --> 00:53:20.670
At the end of the scene, we improvised all of that.
在戏的结尾，所有这些都是我们即兴发挥的。

1065
00:53:20.670 --> 00:53:23.230
And when I was watching it, I was remembering that.
当我看着它的时候，我想起了这一点。

1066
00:53:23.350 --> 00:53:29.710
And then I went to the DVD commentary and Ken Kwapis said, yeah, he was like, the scene didn't really have an ending.
然后我去听了DVD评论音轨，肯·夸皮斯说，是的，他说，这场戏其实没有一个真正的结尾。

1067
00:53:29.990 --> 00:53:34.490
So I just asked the accountants if they would improvise sort of reacting to Michael.
所以我只是让会计们即兴做出对迈克尔的反应。

1068
00:53:34.730 --> 00:53:36.650
And that's how we went out of the scene.
这就是我们拍完这场戏的方式。

1069
00:53:37.290 --> 00:53:43.530
I think this scene is such a great example of the three of you as an improvisational trio.
我觉得这个场景很好地展现了你们三个人作为即兴表演三重奏的默契。

1070
00:53:44.110 --> 00:53:47.450
You guys work so well off of one another.
你们三个配合得太好了。

1071
00:53:47.450 --> 00:53:50.510
Your deliveries are spot on.
你们的台词处理恰到好处。

1072
00:53:50.710 --> 00:53:54.910
And I noted it when I watched it, Angela, and I went to the script.
安吉拉，我看的时候就注意到了，然后我去查了剧本。

1073
00:53:55.190 --> 00:53:57.370
And Ken Kwapis is right.
肯·夸皮斯说得对。

1074
00:53:57.690 --> 00:54:03.230
It really just ended with Michael giving the news that he's already sold his condo on eBay.
剧本本来真的只是以迈克尔宣布他在eBay上卖掉了公寓作为结尾。

1075
00:54:03.450 --> 00:54:04.250
That was the button.
这就是那个收尾的包袱。

1076
00:54:04.550 --> 00:54:09.370
But I think this scene is brilliant because of your reaction.
但我认为这个场景之所以精彩，是因为你们的反应。

1077
00:54:09.410 --> 00:54:11.210
And I'm so glad they left it in.
我很高兴他们把这个保留了下来的。

1078
00:54:11.210 --> 00:54:12.890
Well, I love that it made it in.
嗯，我很高兴它最终播出了。

1079
00:54:12.970 --> 00:54:15.770
And I really loved our little accounting pod.
我真的很喜欢我们那个小的会计小组。

1080
00:54:15.950 --> 00:54:20.790
We so clearly knew our characters and how they would react to one another at all times.
我们非常清楚自己的角色，以及他们在任何时候会对彼此做出什么反应。

1081
00:54:21.010 --> 00:54:24.350
And we were rarely ever on the same page.
而且我们很少意见一致。

1082
00:54:24.530 --> 00:54:28.110
But in this moment, all three of us have similar reactions.
但在这一刻，我们三个人的反应却出奇地一致。

1083
00:54:28.370 --> 00:54:30.490
I say, who gave you that advice?
我说，谁给你的建议？

1084
00:54:30.730 --> 00:54:33.310
You know, and then Kevin and Oscar all chime in.
你知道的，然后凯文和奥斯卡都插话了。

1085
00:54:33.470 --> 00:54:38.550
And for once, the accounting department is all on the same page.
破天荒地，会计部门难得意见完全一致。

1086
00:54:38.550 --> 00:54:47.090
Well, we had a fan catch in this that I absolutely love from Adalia L., who said,
嗯，我们在其中发现了一个粉丝的细心观察，我非常喜欢，来自阿达利亚·L，她说，

1087
00:54:48.250 --> 00:54:54.110
You guys have mentioned that Phyllis was constantly looking at fences for her home.
你们提到过菲利斯经常在看她家的栅栏。

1088
00:54:54.170 --> 00:54:56.990
Please tell me she caught the fence on her computer.
请告诉我她真的在电脑上看栅栏了。

1089
00:54:57.510 --> 00:55:05.250
At about 7 minutes 20 seconds, I think she's looking at fences on her computer in the background of the scene.
在大约7分20秒的时候，我觉得她在背景的场景里看电脑上的栅栏。

1090
00:55:08.160 --> 00:55:10.000
Angela, this is amazing.
安吉拉，这太神奇了。

1091
00:55:11.400 --> 00:55:16.200
Because you know how you were mentioning that sometimes you would check to see if you were in the background?
因为你知道你之前提到过，有时你会检查自己是否在背景里吗？

1092
00:55:16.680 --> 00:55:16.820
Yeah.
是的。

1093
00:55:18.080 --> 00:55:24.300
At 7 minutes 10 seconds, Phyllis looks over her shoulder to accounting.
在7分10秒时，菲利斯转过头看会计部。

1094
00:55:24.560 --> 00:55:29.600
And I swear that what she's doing is sneaking a look to see where the camera is.
我发誓她当时在偷偷看摄像机在哪里。

1095
00:55:29.600 --> 00:55:36.600
And I think she thinks she's not on camera because right after that, she clicks on a website to look at fences.
而且我想她觉得自己没被拍进镜头，因为紧接着她就点进了一个看栅栏的网站。

1096
00:55:37.020 --> 00:55:37.580
Yes!
没错！

1097
00:55:37.800 --> 00:55:39.820
That's exactly what she was doing!
她当时就是在干这个！

1098
00:55:40.100 --> 00:55:40.660
Yes!
没错！

1099
00:55:40.780 --> 00:55:41.660
It was amazing!
太惊艳了！

1100
00:55:41.940 --> 00:55:45.660
You guys, Phyllis looked at fences for like a year.
各位，菲利斯看栅栏看了一年左右。

1101
00:55:46.220 --> 00:55:46.700
Yeah.
是啊。

1102
00:55:47.000 --> 00:55:49.100
Like for months and months.
就像好几个月一样。

1103
00:55:49.420 --> 00:55:52.800
And we would, you know, she would want our opinion.
而且我们会，你知道的，她会想要听听我们的意见。

1104
00:55:52.800 --> 00:55:55.260
And we'd go over and we'd look at fences with her.
我们会过去，跟她一起看栅栏。

1105
00:55:55.960 --> 00:55:56.520
Yeah.
是啊。

1106
00:55:56.840 --> 00:55:57.580
So many fences.
好多栅栏。

1107
00:55:57.680 --> 00:55:57.800
It was great.
太棒了。

1108
00:55:57.800 --> 00:55:58.600
So many fences.
好多栅栏。

1109
00:55:59.360 --> 00:56:07.640
Well, now, Angela, speaking of scenes that I just absolutely love, this next one with Dwight and Angela in the kitchen.
好了，安吉拉，说到我绝对大爱的场景，接下来这个是德怀特和安吉拉在厨房的戏。

1110
00:56:08.020 --> 00:56:11.760
And Dwight is telling Angela about his new promotion.
德怀特正在跟安吉拉讲述他晋升的新消息。

1111
00:56:12.060 --> 00:56:14.120
He is going to have Michael's job.
他要接替迈克尔的工作了。

1112
00:56:15.660 --> 00:56:17.140
Oh, it's so good.
哦，太精彩了。

1113
00:56:17.240 --> 00:56:17.840
It's so good.
太精彩了。

1114
00:56:18.040 --> 00:56:21.440
It's one of these Shakespearean moments between Dwight and Angela.
这是德怀特和安吉拉之间极具莎士比亚风格的时刻之一。

1115
00:56:22.000 --> 00:56:23.140
Very Macbeth, right?
很有《麦克白》的感觉，对吧？

1116
00:56:23.480 --> 00:56:24.040
Yes.
是的。

1117
00:56:24.040 --> 00:56:27.440
And once again, they're not facing each other, you know?
而且又一次，他们没有面对面，你知道吗？

1118
00:56:27.440 --> 00:56:29.820
So Angela doesn't even see his face.
所以安吉拉甚至看不到他的脸。

1119
00:56:30.260 --> 00:56:35.980
And at the end, Angela, you say, goodbye, Kelly Kapoor.
然后在最后，安吉拉，你说，再见，凯莉·卡普尔。

1120
00:56:36.400 --> 00:56:37.000
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1121
00:56:37.120 --> 00:56:39.140
And that was not in the script, lady.
那可不在剧本里，女士。

1122
00:56:39.420 --> 00:56:40.360
I know.
我知道。

1123
00:56:40.500 --> 00:56:40.860
I know.
我知道。

1124
00:56:40.860 --> 00:56:43.940
So I got to improvise a little bit right there.
所以我当时就即兴发挥了一小下。

1125
00:56:43.940 --> 00:56:46.820
And my memory is that I improvised that.
我的记忆是那是我即兴发挥的。

1126
00:56:46.980 --> 00:56:51.560
And when I listened to the DVD commentary, Dave Rogers said, I'm pretty sure Angela improvised that line.
当我听DVD评论音轨时，戴夫·罗杰斯说，我敢肯定那是安吉拉即兴发挥的台词。

1127
00:56:52.060 --> 00:56:56.060
So I just figured she would just be consumed with her own power.
所以我只是觉得她会完全沉浸在自己的权力中。

1128
00:56:56.060 --> 00:57:00.680
And, you know, Dwight has said if he takes over, she gets to be in charge of the women.
而且，你知道，德怀特说过如果他接手，她就能负责管女员工。

1129
00:57:00.860 --> 00:57:02.360
So it's sort of a callback.
所以这算是一个前后呼应。

1130
00:57:03.320 --> 00:57:06.840
And, you know, Kelly Kapoor has been on her list for a long time.
而且，你知道，凯莉·卡普尔在她黑名单上很久了。

1131
00:57:07.240 --> 00:57:10.160
Well, I think this is also a callback to product recall.
嗯，我觉得这也是对“产品召回”那一集的呼应。

1132
00:57:10.380 --> 00:57:16.500
I think that Kelly went to the top of Angela's list after she had to sit through that customer service training.
我觉得凯莉是在不得不熬过那场客服培训后，才冲到了安吉拉黑名单的榜首。

1133
00:57:16.500 --> 00:57:17.480
Well, no doubt.
那毫无疑问。

1134
00:57:17.660 --> 00:57:18.120
No doubt.
毫无疑问。

1135
00:57:18.260 --> 00:57:20.380
She tried to kiss Dwight at a Christmas party.
她曾在圣诞派对上试图亲吻德怀特。

1136
00:57:21.160 --> 00:57:24.480
And then there was Diwali and then product recall.
然后还有排灯节，接着是产品召回。

1137
00:57:24.740 --> 00:57:27.040
So Angela's like, see you later, Kelly Kapoor.
所以安吉拉就觉得，回头见啦，凯莉·卡普尔。

1138
00:57:27.360 --> 00:57:27.600
Yeah.
是啊。

1139
00:57:27.840 --> 00:57:29.420
Who's next on Angela's list?
安吉拉黑名单上下一个是谁？

1140
00:57:29.540 --> 00:57:30.800
Oh, the list is long, lady.
哦，名单很长呢，女士。

1141
00:57:31.000 --> 00:57:31.840
The list is long.
名单很长。

1142
00:57:32.040 --> 00:57:32.090
Is it Kevin?
是凯文吗？

1143
00:57:32.660 --> 00:57:33.420
Maybe Kevin.
也许是凯文。

1144
00:57:33.640 --> 00:57:34.820
Oh, for sure.
哦，肯定的。

1145
00:57:35.040 --> 00:57:35.780
For sure.
肯定的。

1146
00:57:36.800 --> 00:57:40.620
And maybe she gets her way in the finale just saying, okay, we're not there yet.
也许她在结局里如愿以偿了，好吧，我们还没聊到那儿。

1147
00:57:41.000 --> 00:57:41.440
Okay.
好的。

1148
00:57:41.760 --> 00:57:45.380
Well, in this scene, Dwight and Angela have this really fun couplet of dialogue.
嗯，在这个场景里，德怀特和安吉拉有一段非常有趣的对白。

1149
00:57:46.220 --> 00:57:50.800
Dwight says, how would you like to spend the night with a regional manager of Dunder Mifflin Scranton?
德怀特说，你想不想和邓德米弗林斯克兰分公司的地区经理共度良宵？

1150
00:57:50.980 --> 00:57:52.160
And Angela goes, no, Dwight.
然后安吉拉说，不要，德怀特。

1151
00:57:52.280 --> 00:57:55.960
And I don't care if that's how they consolidated power in ancient Rome.
我才不管古代罗马是不是靠这招巩固政权的。

1152
00:57:57.080 --> 00:57:58.960
And he's like, I mean me.
然后他的意思是，指代我。

1153
00:58:00.360 --> 00:58:03.680
Well, listen, lady, I think maybe we should take a break.
听着，女士，我觉得也许我们该休息一下。

1154
00:58:03.680 --> 00:58:09.840
And when we come back, we're going to see what this new power does to Dwight.
等我们回来后，来看看这个新权力会对德怀特产生什么影响。

1155
00:58:10.860 --> 00:58:13.540
Oh, well, get ready.
哦，好吧，准备好吧。

1156
00:58:13.540 --> 00:58:15.800
Get ready for his bed and breakfast in Hill.
准备好迎接地狱山庄民宿吧。

1157
00:58:17.100 --> 00:58:17.940
All right.
好的。

1158
00:58:18.100 --> 00:58:19.300
We'll be right back.
我们马上回来。

1159
00:58:28.190 --> 00:58:28.730
All right.
好的。

1160
00:58:28.870 --> 00:58:29.750
We are back.
我们回来了。

1161
00:58:29.970 --> 00:58:36.390
And Dwight is taunting Jim about his new position at Hotel Hill.
德怀特正在拿他在地狱山庄的新职位嘲笑吉姆。

1162
00:58:36.770 --> 00:58:40.930
And he's doing one of those hand, what are they called?
而且他在摆弄那种手部……叫什么来着？

1163
00:58:41.390 --> 00:58:43.170
Those hand exerciser things.
那种手部锻炼器。

1164
00:58:43.350 --> 00:58:44.410
What are those for?
那到底是干什么用的？

1165
00:58:44.550 --> 00:58:46.470
Why am I exercising my hand?
我为什么要锻炼手部？

1166
00:58:46.470 --> 00:58:48.110
So your grip gets really strong.
这样你的握力就会变得非常强。

1167
00:58:48.550 --> 00:58:51.810
So I can hold heavier weights while I'm lifting weights.
这样我在举重时就能拿更重的杠铃。

1168
00:58:51.950 --> 00:58:52.970
Is that what that's for?
那就是它的用途吗？

1169
00:58:53.510 --> 00:58:54.290
Or maybe.
或者也许吧。

1170
00:58:54.590 --> 00:58:55.890
What do I need a strong hand for?
我为什么需要一双强壮的手？

1171
00:58:56.050 --> 00:58:59.790
Maybe if you wrestle, you can grab someone and hold real tight.
也许如果你摔跤，你可以抓住别人并死死握住。

1172
00:59:00.090 --> 00:59:00.730
I don't know.
我不知道。

1173
00:59:01.810 --> 00:59:02.550
I don't.
我不知道。

1174
00:59:02.650 --> 00:59:07.490
I've never understood why I would want my hands to be super muscularly.
我从来不明白为什么我想让双手变得超级……肌肉发达。

1175
00:59:08.110 --> 00:59:08.630
Muscularly?
肌肉发达地？

1176
00:59:08.790 --> 00:59:09.310
Muscular.
肌肉发达。

1177
00:59:09.630 --> 00:59:11.630
I feel like my husband has one.
我觉得我丈夫有一个。

1178
00:59:11.890 --> 00:59:18.110
And I know with baking, like he's kneading all kinds of dough and bread and doing stuff.
我知道在烘焙时，比如他要揉各种面团和面包之类的东西。

1179
00:59:18.110 --> 00:59:20.910
And I feel like he's got real strong hands.
我觉得他的手非常有力。

1180
00:59:22.670 --> 00:59:23.710
Oh, wow.
哦，哇。

1181
00:59:23.830 --> 00:59:24.910
Do I need one of those?
我需要一个那种东西吗？

1182
00:59:25.050 --> 00:59:25.350
Maybe.
也许吧。

1183
00:59:25.650 --> 00:59:26.950
So that I can knead my dough better?
这样我就能更好地揉面团了？

1184
00:59:26.950 --> 00:59:27.710
Eh, maybe.
呃，也许吧。

1185
00:59:28.030 --> 00:59:31.170
Then you'd have like super dough-neating strength.
那样你就会拥有超级揉面团的力量了。

1186
00:59:32.290 --> 00:59:32.730
Hmm.
嗯。

1187
00:59:33.230 --> 00:59:33.610
Anyway.
总之。

1188
00:59:33.690 --> 00:59:36.390
Maybe I should ask for one for Christmas.
也许我应该在圣诞节讨要一个。

1189
00:59:37.010 --> 00:59:41.950
Dwight is doing this throughout this whole ridiculous, I don't even know what it is,
德怀特在整个荒谬的过程中都在这么做，我甚至不知道那是什么，

1190
00:59:42.050 --> 00:59:45.410
a dream or fantasy of his, of this insane hotel hell.
他的梦想或幻想，关于这个疯狂的地狱酒店。

1191
00:59:45.590 --> 00:59:48.850
And then Jim just takes him to task so calmly.
然后吉姆就那么平静地数落了他。

1192
00:59:49.410 --> 00:59:51.730
He's like, wait, wait, you're the manager?
他说，等等，等等，你是经理？

1193
00:59:51.990 --> 00:59:53.030
You don't, this is your fantasy?
你没……这是你的幻想？

1194
00:59:53.030 --> 00:59:53.910
You don't even own it?
你甚至都不拥有它？

1195
00:59:53.930 --> 00:59:56.170
And he's like, I co-own it with Satan.
他说，我和撒旦共同拥有它。

1196
00:59:57.290 --> 00:59:57.730
Yeah.
是啊。

1197
00:59:58.130 --> 01:00:03.890
And he's like, I just want to make sure I'm clear that your wildest fantasy has you as
他说，我只想弄清楚，你最疯狂的幻想竟然是

1198
01:00:03.890 --> 01:00:07.470
the co-owner of a bed and breakfast with Satan in hell.
在地狱里和撒旦共同经营一家民宿。

1199
01:00:07.710 --> 01:00:10.290
And, but you only make $80,000 a year.
而且，你一年只赚八万美元。

1200
01:00:10.450 --> 01:00:10.670
Oh yeah.
哦，是的。

1201
01:00:10.730 --> 01:00:11.410
Dwight's like, wait, wait, wait.
德怀特就像是，等等，等等，等等。

1202
01:00:11.410 --> 01:00:12.470
I haven't told you the best part.
我还没告诉你最棒的部分呢。

1203
01:00:13.410 --> 01:00:13.850
Yeah.
对。

1204
01:00:14.250 --> 01:00:14.670
Best part.
最棒的部分。

1205
01:00:14.790 --> 01:00:16.150
I make $80,000 a year.
我一年挣八万美元。

1206
01:00:16.730 --> 01:00:17.130
Now, Jenna.
听着，珍娜。

1207
01:00:17.790 --> 01:00:18.890
So here's the thing.
所以事情是这样的。

1208
01:00:18.890 --> 01:00:26.590
I, I saw online that fans of The Office were like, you know, if you divide 80,000 by 12,
我，我在网上看到《办公室》的粉丝们就说，你知道的，如果你把八万除以十二，

1209
01:00:26.890 --> 01:00:31.610
you get like 6666.666667 or something like that.
你会得到大概6666.666667或者类似的数字。

1210
01:00:31.750 --> 01:00:34.070
And I was like, oh my God, do the writers do that on purpose?
然后我就想，天哪，编剧们是故意的吗？

1211
01:00:34.950 --> 01:00:35.890
They must have.
他们肯定是。

1212
01:00:35.930 --> 01:00:36.770
They had to have.
他们一定是的。

1213
01:00:36.930 --> 01:00:37.230
They must have.
他们肯定是。

1214
01:00:37.410 --> 01:00:40.370
Well, what a brilliant little layer they gave that then.
哇，那他们当时设计了一个多棒的小彩蛋啊。

1215
01:00:40.570 --> 01:00:42.230
We had a lot of people write in about that.
我们有很多人写信来谈论这件事。

1216
01:00:42.230 --> 01:00:49.390
Rebecca Womack, Beth Jones, and Paulina Jay and Jake Moss all also noticed that $80,000
丽贝卡·沃马克、贝丝·琼斯、保利娜·杰以及杰克·莫斯也都注意到每年八万

1217
01:00:49.390 --> 01:00:52.910
a year is $6,666.66.
美元就是6666.66美元。

1218
01:00:53.590 --> 01:00:54.490
That's pretty cool.
这挺酷的。

1219
01:00:54.890 --> 01:00:57.630
I mean, that's a little, I mean, I like little details like that.
我的意思是，这有点，我是说，我喜欢这样的小细节。

1220
01:00:57.750 --> 01:00:58.430
I think that's fun.
我觉得这挺有意思的。

1221
01:00:58.790 --> 01:01:03.250
You know, if that were my salary, I think I would be a little bit weirded out.
你知道，如果那是我的薪水，我想我会觉得有点诡异。

1222
01:01:03.470 --> 01:01:05.490
I don't think I would want to have a salary.
我觉得我不会想要有这样的薪水。

1223
01:01:05.650 --> 01:01:06.770
I wouldn't want to get checks.
我可不想收到那样的支票。

1224
01:01:07.270 --> 01:01:09.710
I mean, I guess you take out the taxes and everything.
我的意思是，我猜你要扣除税款和各种费用。

1225
01:01:10.030 --> 01:01:11.330
Your check wouldn't really say that.
你的支票上其实不会写那个数字。

1226
01:01:11.330 --> 01:01:13.870
But even still in my mind, I think it would weird me out.
但即便如此，在我的脑海里，我觉得它还是会让我觉得毛骨悚然。

1227
01:01:14.430 --> 01:01:17.190
Because do you know what I had for a very long time?
因为你知道我有一件东西用了很长时间吗？

1228
01:01:18.350 --> 01:01:18.790
What?
什么？

1229
01:01:19.010 --> 01:01:19.290
What?
什么？

1230
01:01:19.970 --> 01:01:21.370
I had a credit card.
我有一张信用卡。

1231
01:01:21.570 --> 01:01:24.830
And you know, you have your little three digit secret code.
你知道的，你有一个三位数的秘密验证码。

1232
01:01:26.290 --> 01:01:28.650
My secret code was 666.
我的密码是666。

1233
01:01:29.210 --> 01:01:30.350
Oh, no, no, no.
哦，不，不，不。

1234
01:01:30.550 --> 01:01:31.550
I'd say get that away.
我会说把它拿开。

1235
01:01:31.850 --> 01:01:33.310
I'm not having any of that.
我可不想要这种东西。

1236
01:01:33.770 --> 01:01:36.310
I would be on the phone trying to buy something.
我会在电话里尝试买东西。

1237
01:01:37.110 --> 01:01:39.230
Like, let's say I'm ordering a pizza.
比方说，假设我在订披萨。

1238
01:01:39.510 --> 01:01:41.210
And they'd be like, what's your credit card?
然后他们会问，你的信用卡号是多少？

1239
01:01:41.210 --> 01:01:43.250
And they'd be like, and the security code?
然后他们会问，还有安全码呢？

1240
01:01:43.370 --> 01:01:47.950
And I would always be like, it's 666.
我总是会说，是666。

1241
01:01:48.510 --> 01:01:49.550
And what would they say?
然后他们会说什么？

1242
01:01:50.630 --> 01:01:52.070
People would be like, what?
人们会说，什么？

1243
01:01:52.410 --> 01:01:53.550
They would laugh.
他们会笑。

1244
01:01:53.730 --> 01:01:56.770
It was, and I'd always have to be like, I know, I know.
那是，而且我总是不得不说，我知道，我知道。

1245
01:01:57.350 --> 01:02:02.430
And I wanted to like, just intentionally get rid of this card.
我想，就是故意把这张卡扔掉。

1246
01:02:02.430 --> 01:02:03.870
So they would issue me a new one.
这样他们就会给我补发一张新的。

1247
01:02:04.110 --> 01:02:05.990
Now, that's not my security code anymore.
现在，那已经不是我的安全码了。

1248
01:02:05.990 --> 01:02:11.710
But I imagine that's like layered because it's like, on the one hand, that's creepy.
但我可以想象这就好像是有层次的，因为一方面，这很吓人。

1249
01:02:12.090 --> 01:02:12.870
It's creepy.
这很吓人。

1250
01:02:13.070 --> 01:02:14.530
And then you have to say these creepy numbers.
然后你还得说出这些吓人的数字。

1251
01:02:14.690 --> 01:02:17.910
But then you also now have chitty chat.
但现在你又得闲聊。

1252
01:02:18.130 --> 01:02:20.150
When you just want to order your pizza.
当你只是想点个披萨的时候。

1253
01:02:21.250 --> 01:02:23.630
Now, that person's hearing it for the first time.
现在，那个人是第一次听到。

1254
01:02:23.730 --> 01:02:25.250
So they're like, oh, my God, that's weird.
所以他们会觉得，天哪，这太奇怪了。

1255
01:02:25.350 --> 01:02:26.030
Yeah, I know.
对，我知道。

1256
01:02:26.250 --> 01:02:27.690
Oh, are you going to change it?
哦，你要改掉它吗？

1257
01:02:27.770 --> 01:02:28.490
I'm going to try.
我尽量。

1258
01:02:28.490 --> 01:02:30.990
But like over and over for two years.
但就像这样持续了整整两年。

1259
01:02:31.290 --> 01:02:31.710
For two years.
整整两年。

1260
01:02:32.110 --> 01:02:34.170
Well, then Dwight has a talking head.
好吧，然后德怀特有一个访谈镜头。

1261
01:02:34.330 --> 01:02:40.510
He says his first order of business will be to demote Jim, which means he will need a new number two.
他说他上任后的第一件事就是降职吉姆，这意味着他需要一个新的副手。

1262
01:02:40.730 --> 01:02:42.910
His first choice would be Jack Bauer.
他的首选会是杰克·鲍尔。

1263
01:02:43.110 --> 01:02:43.670
Yeah.
是啊。

1264
01:02:43.790 --> 01:02:44.530
You know, from 24.
你知道的，来自《24小时》。

1265
01:02:44.870 --> 01:02:46.690
But he's fictional and unavailable.
但他是个虚构人物，而且没空。

1266
01:02:47.050 --> 01:02:50.210
This was a nod to Ricky Gervais and Stephen Merchant.
这是对瑞奇·热维斯和斯蒂芬·莫钱特的致敬。

1267
01:02:51.130 --> 01:02:52.010
How so?
怎么说？

1268
01:02:52.550 --> 01:02:54.870
They loved 24.
他们超爱《24小时》。

1269
01:02:55.570 --> 01:02:56.530
Loved 24.
超爱《24小时》。

1270
01:02:56.770 --> 01:02:58.190
They were obsessed with it.
他们对它痴迷不已。

1271
01:02:58.190 --> 01:03:01.310
They both got cameos on 24.
他们俩都在《24小时》里客串过。

1272
01:03:01.810 --> 01:03:02.530
I went.
我去了。

1273
01:03:02.610 --> 01:03:02.790
What?
什么？

1274
01:03:02.910 --> 01:03:03.290
Yes.
是的。

1275
01:03:03.450 --> 01:03:04.330
And I watched them.
我还看着他们拍的。

1276
01:03:04.690 --> 01:03:07.010
So Ricky Gervais was in the sixth season.
所以瑞奇·热维斯出演了第六季。

1277
01:03:07.210 --> 01:03:08.590
His scene did not make it.
他的戏份被剪掉了。

1278
01:03:08.790 --> 01:03:10.410
But you can find it online.
但你可以在网上找到。

1279
01:03:10.410 --> 01:03:13.010
And I guess it's on like the DVD box set or something.
我猜它大概也在DVD套装之类的东西里。

1280
01:03:13.590 --> 01:03:16.450
And he's having this comedic moment in the Oval Office.
他在椭圆形办公室里有一个搞笑的时刻。

1281
01:03:16.610 --> 01:03:17.590
It's totally random.
这完全是突如其来的。

1282
01:03:17.590 --> 01:03:19.350
Because, you know, 24 is such a drama.
因为你知道，《24小时》是一部正剧。

1283
01:03:19.490 --> 01:03:20.690
The stakes are so high.
局势极其紧迫。

1284
01:03:20.930 --> 01:03:24.930
But he's in the background with his longtime girlfriend, Jane Fallon.
但他在背景里，和他的多年女友简·法伦在一起。

1285
01:03:25.090 --> 01:03:26.290
They got to be in the show.
他们得以参演这部剧。

1286
01:03:26.290 --> 01:03:30.330
And then later on, Stephen Merchant makes a brief appearance.
然后后来，斯蒂芬·莫钱特也短暂客串了一下。

1287
01:03:30.570 --> 01:03:32.010
He doesn't have a speaking role.
他没有台词。

1288
01:03:32.010 --> 01:03:34.110
But he's a CTU worker.
但他是个反恐局工作人员。

1289
01:03:34.790 --> 01:03:36.310
He wasn't credited on the episode.
他在这一集中没有署名。

1290
01:03:36.410 --> 01:03:37.050
But he is there.
但他确实在那里。

1291
01:03:37.150 --> 01:03:39.130
He's in the background when they cut to CTU.
当镜头切换到反恐局时，他在背景里。

1292
01:03:39.650 --> 01:03:40.810
So he made it in.
所以他成功出镜了。

1293
01:03:40.870 --> 01:03:41.550
He made it in.
他成功出镜了。

1294
01:03:41.750 --> 01:03:42.690
He has no lines.
他一句台词也没有。

1295
01:03:42.790 --> 01:03:43.390
But he made it in.
但他成功出镜了。

1296
01:03:43.510 --> 01:03:50.410
But I guess this little reference to Jack Bauer from Dwight was a little nod to Ricky and Stephen from the writers.
但我想编剧们让德怀特提到杰克·鲍尔这个小彩蛋，是对瑞奇和斯蒂芬的一点致敬。

1297
01:03:51.290 --> 01:03:52.410
I love that.
我太喜欢这个了。

1298
01:03:52.850 --> 01:03:56.190
Well, now something major happens.
好了，现在有大事发生了。

1299
01:03:56.970 --> 01:03:58.630
Two major things happen.
两件大事发生了。

1300
01:03:59.170 --> 01:04:01.510
Jan shows up at the office unannounced.
简不请自来到办公室了。

1301
01:04:01.630 --> 01:04:08.310
And we talked about this scene a little bit with Paul, where Jan and Michael are standing at reception with Pam between them.
我们和保罗稍微聊过这个场景，简和迈克尔站在前台，帕姆在他们中间。

1302
01:04:08.590 --> 01:04:11.250
And Michael is trying so hard to have boundaries.
迈克尔极力想要划清界限。

1303
01:04:11.250 --> 01:04:16.710
Oh, I loved it when she walked in and he goes, why are you here?
哦，我太喜欢她走进来时他说，你为什么来？

1304
01:04:18.550 --> 01:04:25.870
And Melora is being that very, very scary, sane version of a crazy person.
梅洛拉演出了那种极其可怕、看似神志正常的疯子状态。

1305
01:04:26.270 --> 01:04:27.790
Oh, for sure.
哦，绝对是。

1306
01:04:28.090 --> 01:04:30.390
Like in the horror movies, right before they turn on you.
就像恐怖电影里，在他们对你翻脸之前那样。

1307
01:04:30.550 --> 01:04:30.710
Yeah.
对。

1308
01:04:30.870 --> 01:04:34.290
No, it's that moment where you're like, hi, lovely.
不，就是那种你觉得，嗨，亲爱的，的时刻。

1309
01:04:34.750 --> 01:04:35.550
And then it's like, ah.
然后紧接着就是，啊。

1310
01:04:36.290 --> 01:04:39.930
Yes, like you're wondering, wait, are they a cyborg?
没错，就像你在想，等等，他们是生化人吗？

1311
01:04:40.190 --> 01:04:40.330
Yeah.
对。

1312
01:04:40.570 --> 01:04:42.310
I made you coffee, honey.
我给你煮了咖啡，亲爱的。

1313
01:04:42.650 --> 01:04:43.550
Wah, wah, wah.
哇，哇，哇。

1314
01:04:43.710 --> 01:04:44.130
With the knife.
拿着刀。

1315
01:04:44.250 --> 01:04:44.610
Yes.
是的。

1316
01:04:44.790 --> 01:04:44.970
Yes.
是的。

1317
01:04:45.370 --> 01:04:45.790
Yes.
是的。

1318
01:04:46.030 --> 01:04:46.830
Super creepy.
超级诡异。

1319
01:04:47.670 --> 01:04:54.130
She goes into his office and Michael is like, I need all my ladies.
她走进他的办公室，迈克尔说，我需要我所有的女士们。

1320
01:04:54.450 --> 01:04:55.030
Def content.
防务内容。

1321
01:04:55.550 --> 01:04:56.130
In the conference room.
在会议室。

1322
01:04:56.330 --> 01:04:57.270
Def content, Pam.
防务内容，帕姆。

1323
01:04:58.410 --> 01:04:58.970
Immediately.
马上。

1324
01:04:59.730 --> 01:05:01.510
Except Meredith, who's an alternate.
除了梅雷迪思，她是个替补。

1325
01:05:01.790 --> 01:05:01.890
Yeah.
对。

1326
01:05:02.930 --> 01:05:05.910
Well, so now Pam has to go tell everybody, right?
好吧，现在帕姆得去告诉大家，对吧？

1327
01:05:06.010 --> 01:05:08.650
So she goes up to Karen and she's like, hey, Michael needs us.
所以她走向凯伦说，嘿，迈克尔需要我们。

1328
01:05:08.790 --> 01:05:09.350
Jan's here.
简来了。

1329
01:05:09.490 --> 01:05:10.290
He's freaking out.
他快抓狂了。

1330
01:05:10.610 --> 01:05:14.710
And Karen is so passive aggressive in this moment.
凯伦在这个时候表现得太消极抵抗了。

1331
01:05:14.970 --> 01:05:22.090
She's like, okay, listen, before we leave, would you make copies of our sales reports?
她就像是，好吧，听着，在我们离开之前，你能复印一下我们的销售报告吗？

1332
01:05:22.370 --> 01:05:23.470
Would you go make some copies?
你能去复印一些东西吗？

1333
01:05:23.630 --> 01:05:26.070
Would you photocopy some stuff for me?
能帮我复印点东西吗？

1334
01:05:26.350 --> 01:05:30.030
Oh, and for my boyfriend, whom I'm about to go to New York with for the night.
哦，还有为了我即将一起去纽约过夜的男朋友。

1335
01:05:30.190 --> 01:05:31.770
Will you make us some photocopy?
你能给我们复印一下吗？

1336
01:05:32.790 --> 01:05:33.930
That's the subtext.
这就是潜台词。

1337
01:05:34.190 --> 01:05:34.490
Yeah.
对。

1338
01:05:35.030 --> 01:05:35.750
I know.
我知道。

1339
01:05:35.870 --> 01:05:38.630
I'm just going to, I'm going to take a minute and I'm going to put you in your place,
我只想，我要花点时间，把你的气焰压下去，

1340
01:05:39.030 --> 01:05:39.970
Miss ReceptioniSt.
前台小姐。

1341
01:05:40.530 --> 01:05:41.570
Yeah, she does.
对，她确实这么做了。

1342
01:05:42.050 --> 01:05:42.830
It's true.
确实如此。

1343
01:05:43.130 --> 01:05:48.830
And then though, Pam, Pam leaning hard into this new, like, I'm going to say stuff when
然后呢，帕姆，帕姆坚定地展现出这种新的态度，就是，我想说什么就说什么，

1344
01:05:48.830 --> 01:05:53.530
I want to say it, looks right at her and goes, I hope you get the job.
直视着她说，我希望你得到这份工作。

1345
01:05:53.770 --> 01:05:53.950
Yeah.
对。

1346
01:05:54.430 --> 01:05:55.310
Little Pam sass.
小小的帕姆式傲娇。

1347
01:05:55.510 --> 01:05:57.090
I want your ass out of here.
我希望你快点滚蛋。

1348
01:05:57.090 --> 01:05:58.210
I'll make your copies.
我来帮你复印。

1349
01:05:58.530 --> 01:05:59.230
I want your ass gone.
我希望你消失。

1350
01:05:59.230 --> 01:06:01.230
I'll make you 12 copies.
我给你复印十二份。

1351
01:06:01.590 --> 01:06:02.370
